effective after the close of business on February 18, 2005 ('Closing Date').\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMT II Historical Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMT II is an open-end, management investment company formed as a statutory trust under the laws of the State of Delaware on November 12, 2004, pursuant to a Declaration of Trust dated November 5, 2004. Each of the Funds which are a series of JPMT II were formerly a series of One Group Mutual Funds, a Massachusetts business trust which was formed on May 23, 1985 ('Predecessor OG Funds'). At shareholder meetings held on January 20, 2005 and February 3, 2005, shareholders of One Group Mutual Funds approved the redomiciliation of One Group Mutual Funds as a Delaware statutory trust to be called JPMorgan Trust II. The redomiciliation was effective after the close of business on the closing date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With respect to events that occurred or payments that were made prior to the Closing Date, any reference to Fund(s) in this SAI prior to the Closing Date refers to the Predecessor JPMorgan Funds and the Predecessor OG Funds (collectively the 'Predecessor Funds').\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Funds. After the close of business on February 18, 2005, certain Predecessor JPMorgan Funds and Predecessor OG Funds merged with and into the Funds listed below. The following list identifies the target funds and the surviving funds:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Target Funds                                                                                           Surviving Funds \par One Group Treasury Only Money Market Fund                                                              JPMorgan 100% U.S Treasury Securities Money Market Fund \par One Group U.S. Government Securities Money Market Fund; JPMorgan U.S. Government Money Market Fund     One Group Government Money Market Fund now known as JPMorgan U.S. Government Money Market Fund \par JPMorgan Liquid Assets Money Market Fund                                                               One Group Prime Money Market Fund now known as JPMorgan Liquid Assets Money Market Fund \par JPMorgan Treasury Plus Money Market Fund                                                               One Group U.S. Treasury Securities Money Market Fund now known as JPMorgan U.S. Treasury Plus Money Market Fund \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fund Names. Prior to February 19, 2005, the following Funds were renamed with the approval of the Board of Trustees:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Name                                              Current Name \par One Group Government Money Market Fund                   JPMorgan U.S. Government Money Market Fund \par One Group Municipal Money Market Fund                    JPMorgan Municipal Money Market Fund \par One Group Prime Money Market Fund                        JPMorgan Liquid Assets Money Market Fund \par One Group U.S. Treasury Securities Money Market Fund     JPMorgan U.S. Treasury Plus Money Market Fund \par JPMorgan \f28 \uc2 \f2 California Tax Free Money Market Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2            JPMorgan California Municipal Money Market Fund \par JPMorgan New York Tax Free Money Market Fund             JPMorgan New York Municipal Money Market Fund \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Part I - 1\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Effective September 10, 2001, the Board of Trustees of JPMMFT approved the re-naming of the following Funds:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Name                               Current Name \par JPMorgan Prime Money Market Fund II       JPMorgan Prime Money Market Fund \par JPMorgan Federal Money Market Fund II     JPMorgan Federal Money Market Fund \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Effective May 1, 2003, the Predecessor JPM Trust was renamed with the approval of the Board of Trustees to J.P. Morgan Mutual Fund Trust from Mutual Fund Trust.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMT IV Historical Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMT IV is an open-end, management investment company formed as a statutory trust under the laws of the State of Delaware on November 11, 2015, pursuant to a Declaration of Trust dated November 11, 2015, as subsequently amended. In addition to the Institutional Tax Free Money Market Fund, the Trust consists of other series representing separate investment funds (each a 'J.P. Morgan Fund').\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share Classes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Board of Trustees of JPMT I, JPMT II and JPMT IV has authorized the issuance and sale of the following share classes of the Funds:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fund                                                Academy     Agency     Agency SL     Capital     Class C    E*TradeClass    IMShares    InstitutionalClass \par Institutional Tax Free Money Market Fund                        X                        X                                       X 4         X \par Prime Money Market Fund                             X 1         X                        X           X                           X 4         X \par Securities Lending Money Market Fund                                       X 2                                                               \par 100% U.S. Treasury Securities Money Market Fund                 X                        X                                       X 4         X \par Federal Money Market Fund                                       X                        X*                                                  X \par U.S. Government Money Market Fund                   X 1         X                        X                       X 3             X 4         X \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Plus Money Market Fund                            X                        X*          X                           X 4         X \par California Municipal Money Market Fund                          X                                                X 3                         X \par Liquid Assets Money Market Fund                            