r the Investment Company Act).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9744\'26\'10\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interval Fund (Registered Closed-End Fund or a Business Development Company that makes periodic repurchase offers under Rule 23c-3 under the Investment Company Act).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9746\'26\'12\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A.2 Qualified (qualified to register securities pursuant to General Instruction A.2 of this Form).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9744\'26\'10\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Well-Known Seasoned Issuer (as defined by Rule 405 under the Securities Act).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9744\'26\'10\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Growth Company (as defined by Rule 12b-2 under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 ('Exchange Act').\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9744\'26\'10\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If an Emerging Growth Company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 7(a)(2)(B) of Securities Act.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u9744\'26\'10\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Registrant (registered or regulated under the Investment Company Act for less than 12 calendar months preceding this filing).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CALCULATION OF REGISTRATION FEE UNDER THE SECURITIES ACT OF 1933\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                          \par \par Title of Securities Being Registered       AmountBeingRegistered(1)    ProposedMaximum OfferingPrice Per Unit    Proposed MaximumAggregateOffering Price(2)   Amount ofRegistration Fee(3)\par Common Stock, $0.001 par value per share                                                                         $43,283,467(4)                                $4,722.23 \par                                          \par \par                                          \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are being registered hereunder a presently indeterminate number of shares of com