\par\par \b \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 . - Primary Offering Prospectus (SEC Filing - 424B2)\b0\par\par\uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co. published this content on 26 Apr 2021 and is solely responsible for the information contained herein. Distributed by PUBT, unedited and unaltered, on 26 Apr 2021 10:06:18 UTC. \par \uc2 12,708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2021\par \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Filings\par \uc2 SAEXC\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021. As included in the Information \par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/0001213900-21-022774-index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Original document}}}\par \par \uc2 Primary Offering Prospectus (SEC Filing - 424B2)\par \par \uc2 \f2 Pricing supplementTo prospectus dated April 8, 2020,prospectus supplement dated April 8, 2020 andproduct supplement no. 2-II dated November 4, 2020 Registration Statement Nos. 333-236659 and 333-236659-01Dated April 23, 2021Rule 424(b)(2)\par JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC                                                                 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 $2,000,000\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Return Notes Linked to the Performance of an Equally Weighted Basket of Ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Relative to the U.S. Dollar due May 10, 2022\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fully and Unconditionally Guaranteed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 The notes are designed for investors who seek exposure to the performance of an equally weighted basket of ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar, as increased by the Basket Adjustment Factor, and who believe that the basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate relative to the U.S. dollar from the Pricing Date to the Observation Date. Due to the embedded cap on each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return of approximately 100% described below, the return on the notes at maturity is effectively capped at approximately 112.30%. \u183\'00\'B7 Investors should be willing to forgo interest payments and, if the Basket declines by more than approximately 5.79369%, be willing to lose some or all of their principal amount at maturity. \u183\'00\'B7 The notes are unsecured and unsubordinated obligations of JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC, which we refer to as JPMorgan Financial, the payment on which is fully and unconditionally guaranteed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Any payment on the notes is subject to the credit risk of JPMorgan Financial, as issuer of the notes, and the credit risk of \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as guarantor of the notes. \u183\'00\'B7 Minimum denominations of $10,000 and integral multiples of $1,000 in excess thereof\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Key Terms\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Issuer: JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC, an indirect, wholly owned finance subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Guarantor: \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Basket: An equally weighted basket of ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (each, a 'Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' and together, the 'Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ') that measures the performance of the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar (the 'Base \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ') Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The following table sets forth the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Starting Spot Rate\u8224\'20\'20 and the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Weight for each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Starting Spot Rate\u8224\'20\'20\u8224\'20\'20 Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Weight Indian rupee (INR) \u8224\'20\'20 74.9404 10% Indonesian rupiah (IDR) \u8224\'20\'20 14,530 10% Russian ruble (RUB) \u8224\'20\'20 76.2052 10% Turkish lira (TRY) \u8224\'20\'20 8.29750 10% Offshore Chinese renminbi (CNH) \u8224\'20\'20 6.48610 10% Philippine peso (PHP) \u8224\'20\'20 48.396 10% Colombian peso (COP) \u8224\'20\'20 3,630.81 10% Brazilian real (BRL) \u8224\'20\'20 5.4970 10% Singapore dollar (SGD) \u8224\'20\'20 1.32900 10% New Taiwan dollar (TWD) \u8224\'20\'20 28.0850 10%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8224\'20\'20 The Starting Spot Rate is expressed as a number of units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per one U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8224\'20\'20\u8224\'20\'20 The Starting Spot Rate of each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the Spot Rate of that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the Pricing Date, determined as specified under 'Additional Key Terms - Spot Rate' below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment at Maturity:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment at maturity will reflect the performance of the Basket, subject to the Basket Adjustment Factor. Accordingly, at maturity, you will receive an amount per $1,000 principal amount note calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 $1,000 \u215\'00\'D7 (1 + Basket Return) \u215\'00\'D7 Basket Adjustment Factor\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In no event, however, will the payment at maturity be less than $0.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 You will lose some or all of your principal amount at maturity if the Basket Return reflects a decline in the closing level of the Basket of more than approximately 5.79369%. For more information on how the Basket Adjustment Factor can impact your payment at maturity, please see 'What Is the Total Return on the Notes at Maturity, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Basket?' in this pricing supplement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return formula used to calculate the Basket Return effectively limits the contribution of each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to an approximately 100% return but does not limit any negative contribution of any Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Accordingly, due to the embedded cap on each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return, the return on the notes at maturity is effectively capped at approximately 112.30%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See 'Additional Key Terms - Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return,' 'How Does the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return Formula Work?', 'Selected Risk Considerations - Risks Relating to the Notes Generally - Your Notes Are Subject to an Embedded Maximum Payment at Maturity' and 'What Is the Basket Return, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?' in this pricing supplement for more information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basket Adjustment Factor: 106.15% Pricing Date: April 22, 2021 Original Issue Date: On or about April 27, 2021 (Settlement Date) Observation Date*: May 5, 2022 Maturity Date*: May 10, 2022 CUSIP: 48130UVX0 * Subject to postponement in the event of certain market disruption events and as described under 'General Terms of Notes - Postponement of a Determination Date - Notes Linked to Multiple Underlyings' and 'General Terms of Notes - Postponement of a Payment Date' in the accompanying product supplement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investing in the notes involves a number of risks. See 'Risk Factors' beginning on page S-2 of the accompanying prospectus supplement, 'Risk Factors' beginning on page PS-11 of the accompanying product supplement and 'Selected Risk Considerations' beginning on page PS-9 of this pricing supplement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Neither the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Securities and Exchange Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the 'SEC') nor any state securities commission has approved or disapproved of the notes or passed upon the accuracy or the adequacy of this pricing supplement or the accompanying product supplement, prospectus supplement and prospectus. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2            Price to Public(1)   Fees and Commissions (2)   Proceeds to Issuer \par Per note   $1,000               $7.50                      $992.50 \par Total      $2,000,000           $15,000                    $1,985,000 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1) See 'Supplemental Use of Proceeds' in this pricing supplement for information about the components of the price to public of the notes. (2) \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Securities LLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which we refer to as JPMS, acting as agent for JPMorgan Financial, will pay all of the selling commissions of $7.50 per $1,000 principal amount note it receives from us to other affiliated or unaffiliated dealers. See 'Plan of Distribution (Conflicts of Interest)' in the accompanying product supplement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The estimated value of the notes, when the terms of the notes were set, was $981.80 per $1,000 principal amount note. See 'The Estimated Value of the Notes' in this pricing supplement for additional information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The notes are not bank deposits, are not insured by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  or any other governmental agency and are not obligations of, or guaranteed by, a bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Terms Specific to the Notes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 You should read this pricing supplement together with the accompanying prospectus, as supplemented by the accompanying prospectus supplement relating to our Series A medium-term notes, of which these notes are a part, and the more detailed information contained in the accompanying product supplement. This pricing supplement, together with the documents listed below, contains the terms of the notes and supersedes all other prior or contemporaneous oral statements as well as any other written materials including preliminary or indicative pricing terms, correspondence, trade ideas, structures for implementation, sample structures, fact sheets, brochures or other educational materials of ours. You should carefully consider, among other things, the matters set forth in the 'Risk Factors' sections of the accompanying prospectus supplement and the accompanying product supplement, as the notes involve risks not associated with conventional debt securities. We urge you to consult your investment, legal, tax, accounting and other advisers before you invest in the notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 You may access these documents on the SEC website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sec.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.sec.gov}}}\uc2 \f2  as follows (or if such address has changed, by reviewing our filings for the relevant date on the SEC website):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Product supplement no. 2-II dated November 4, 2020:\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000095010320021465/crt_dp139320-424b2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000095010320021465/crt_dp139320-424b2.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Prospectus supplement and prospectus, each dated April 8, 2020:\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000095010320007214/crt_dp124361-424b2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000095010320007214/crt_dp124361-424b2.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Our Central Index Key, or CIK, on the SEC website is 1665650, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s CIK is 19617. As used in this pricing supplement, 'we,' 'us' and 'our' refer to JPMorgan Financial.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Key Terms\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 BASKET RETURN - The Basket Return reflects the performance of the Basket from the Starting Basket Level to the Ending Basket Level and is calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ending Basket Level - Starting Basket Level\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Starting Basket Level\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 STARTING BASKET LEVEL - The Starting Basket Level is set equal to 100 on the Pricing Date. \u183\'00\'B7 ENDING BASKET LEVEL - The Ending Basket Level is the closing level of the Basket on the Observation Date. \u183\'00\'B7 CLOSING LEVEL OF THE BASKET - The closing level of the Basket on the Observation Date will be calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 100 \u215\'00\'D7 [1 + (INR Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (IDR Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (RUB Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (TRY Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (CNH Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (PHP Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (COP Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (BRL Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (SGD Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%) + (TWD Return \u215\'00\'D7 10%)]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The INR Return, IDR Return, RUB Return, TRY Return, CNH Return, PHP Return, COP Return, BRL Return, SGD Return and TWD Return are the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Returns of the Indian rupee, the Indonesian rupiah, the Russian ruble, the Turkish lira, the offshore Chinese renminbi, the Philippine peso, the Colombian peso, the Brazilian real, the Singapore dollar and the New Taiwan dollar, respectively, on the Observation Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 REFERENCE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RETURN - The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return with respect to each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflects the performance of that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar from its Starting Spot Rate to its Ending Spot Rate. With respect to each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return is calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Starting Spot Rate - Ending Spot Rate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Starting Spot Rate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This formula effectively limits the contribution of each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to an approximately 100% return but do not limit any negative contribution of any Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See 'How Does the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return Formula Work?', 'Selected Risk Considerations - Risks Relating to the Notes Generally - Your Notes Are Subject to an Embedded Maximum Payment at Maturity' and 'What Is the Basket Return, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?' in this pricing supplement for more information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 ENDING SPOT RATE - The Ending Spot Rate with respect to a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the Spot Rate of that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the Observation Date. \u183\'00\'B7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BUSINESS DAY - A '\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business day,' with respect to each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , means a day, as determined by the calculation agent, on which (a) dealings in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in accordance with the practice of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market occur in the City of New York, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 principal financial\f28 \uc2 \f2  center for the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (with respect to the Indian rupee, Mumbai, India; with respect to the Indonesian rupiah, Jakarta, Indonesia; with respect to the Russian ruble, Moscow, Russia; with respect to the Turkish lira, Istanbul, Turkey; with respect to the offshore Chinese renminbi, Hong Kong; with respect to the Philippine peso, Manila, Philippines; with respect to the Colombian peso, Bogot\u225\'00\'E1, Colombia; with respect to the Brazilian real, S\u227\'00\'E3o Paulo, Brazil; with respect to the Singapore dollar, Singapore; and with respect to the New Taiwan dollar, Taipei, Taiwan) and (b) banking institutions in the City of New York and that \f28 \uc2 \f2 principal financial\f28 \uc2 \f2  center for that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are not otherwise authorized or required by law, regulation or executive order to close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Structured Investments -                                                                    PS-1 \par Return Notes Linked to the Performance of an Equally Weighted Basket of Ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Relative to the U.S. Dollar  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 SPOT RATE - With respect to each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Spot Rate on any relevant day is expressed as a number of units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per one U.S. dollar as reported by Refinitiv Ltd. ('Refinitiv') on the page set forth in the table below (or any successor page) at the applicable time set forth in the table below. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Refinitiv Page and Applicable Time \par Indian rupee (INR)                USDINRREF =FBIL, at approximately 1:30 p.m., Calcutta time on the relevant day \par Indonesian rupiah (IDR)           JISDOR=, at approximately 10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the relevant day \par Russian ruble (RUB)               USDFIXME=RTS, at approximately 12:30 p.m. Moscow time on the relevant day \par Turkish lira (TRY)                WMRSPOT07, at approximately 4:00 p.m., Greenwich Mean Time on the relevant day \par Offshore Chinese renminbi (CNH)   WMRSPOT14, at approximately 4:00 p.m., Greenwich Mean Time on the relevant day \par Philippine peso (PHP)             PHPFIX=BAPH, at approximately 11:30 a.m. Manila time on the relevant day \par Colombian peso (COP)              COTCRM=RR, as fixed at approximately 6:00 p.m., Bogota time on the relevant day and published on that page on the business day immediately following the relevant day \par Brazilian real (BRL)              BRLPTAX=CBBR (ask rate), at approximately 1:15 pm Sao Paolo time on the relevant day \par Singapore dollar (SGD)            WMRSPOT13, at approximately 4:00 p.m., Greenwich Mean Time on the relevant day \par New Taiwan dollar (TWD)           TWDFIX=TPFI, at approximately 11:00 a.m. Taipei time on the relevant day \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 How Do Exchange Rates Work?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exchange rates reflect the amount of one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that can be exchanged for a unit of another \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With respect to each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Spot Rate is expressed as a number of units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per one U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 As a result, a decrease in the Spot Rate from the Starting Spot Rate to the Ending Spot Rate means that the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has appreciated / strengthened relative to the U.S. dollar from the Starting Spot Rate to the Ending Spot Rate. This means that one unit of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could purchase more U.S. dollars on the Observation Date than it could on the Pricing Date. Viewed another way, it would take fewer units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to purchase one U.S. dollar on the Observation Date than it did on the Pricing Date. \u183\'00\'B7 Conversely, an increase in the Spot Rate from the Starting Spot Rate to the Ending Spot Rate means that the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has depreciated / weakened relative to the U.S. dollar from the Starting Spot Rate to the Ending Spot Rate. This means that it would take more units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to purchase one U.S. dollar on the Observation Date than it did on the Pricing Date. Viewed another way, one unit of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could purchase fewer U.S. dollars on the Observation Date than it could on the Pricing Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 How Does the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return Formula Work?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return reflects the return of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar from the Starting Spot Rate to the Ending Spot Rate, calculated using the formula set forth above under 'Additional Key Terms - Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return.' While each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return for purposes of the notes is determined using the formula set forth above under 'Additional Key Terms - Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return,' there are other reasonable ways to determine the return of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar that would provide different results. For example, another way to calculate the return of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar would be to calculate the return that would be achieved by converting U.S. dollar into that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the Starting Spot Rate on the Pricing Date and then, on the Observation Date, converting back into U.S. dollar at the applicable Ending Spot Rate. In this pricing supplement, we refer to the return of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar calculated using that method, which is not used for purposes of the notes, as a 'conversion return.'\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As demonstrated by the examples below, under the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return formula, any appreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar will be diminished, as compared to a conversion return, while any depreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar will be magnified, as compared to a conversion return. In addition, the diminishing effect on any appreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar increases as the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return increases, and the magnifying effect on any depreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar increases as the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return decreases. Accordingly, your payment at maturity may be less than if you had invested in similar notes that reflected conversion returns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following examples assume a Starting Spot Rate of 109 for the Indian rupee relative to the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Structured Investments -                                                                    PS-2 \par Return Notes Linked to the Performance of an Equally Weighted Basket of Ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Relative to the U.S. Dollar  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Example 1: The Indian rupee strengthens from the Starting Spot Rate of 75 to the Ending Spot Rate of 67.50.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return is equal to 10.00%, calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (75 - 67.50) / 75 = 10.00%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By contrast, if the return on the Indian rupee were determined using a conversion return, the return would be 11.11%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Example 2: The Indian rupee strengthens from the Starting Spot Rate of 75 to the Ending Spot Rate of 0.75.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return is equal to 99.00%, which demonstrates the effective cap of approximately 100% on the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return, calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (75 - 0.75) / 75 = 99.00%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By contrast, if the return on the Indian rupee were determined using a conversion return, which would not be subject to the effective cap of approximately 100%, the return would be 9,900.00%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As Examples 1 and 2 above demonstrate, the diminishing effect on any appreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the Base \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increases as the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return increases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Example 3: The Indian rupee weakens from the Starting Spot Rate of 75 to the Ending Spot Rate of 82.50.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return is equal to -10.00%, calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (75 - 82.50) / 75 = -10.00%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By contrast, if the return on the Indian rupee were determined using a conversion return, the return would be -9.09%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Example 4: The Indian rupee weakens from the Starting Spot Rate of 75 to the Ending Spot Rate of 300.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return is equal to -300.00%, which demonstrates that there is no limit on the downside for the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return, calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (75 - 300) / 75 = -300.00%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By contrast, if the return on the Indian rupee were determined using a conversion return, the return would be -75.00%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As Examples 3 and 4 above demonstrate, the magnifying effect on any depreciation of a Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the Base \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increases as the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return decreases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The hypothetical Starting Spot Rate, Ending Spot Rates and Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Returns set forth above are for illustrative purposes only and have been rounded for ease of analysis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Structured Investments -                                                                    PS-3 \par Return Notes Linked to the Performance of an Equally Weighted Basket of Ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Relative to the U.S. Dollar  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What Is the Payment at Maturity on the Notes, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Basket?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table and examples illustrate the hypothetical total return and the hypothetical payment at maturity on the notes. The 'total return' as used in this pricing supplement is the number, expressed as a percentage, that results from comparing the payment at maturity per $1,000 principal amount note to $1,000. Each hypothetical total return or payment at maturity set forth below and reflects the Basket Adjustment Factor of 106.15%. Each hypothetical total return or payment at maturity set forth below is for illustrative purposes only and may not be the actual total return or payment at maturity applicable to a purchaser of the notes. The numbers appearing in the following table and in the examples below have been rounded for ease of analysis.\f28 \par \par \