\par\par \b \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 . - Primary Offering Prospectus (SEC Filing - 424B2)\b0\par\par\uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co. published this content on 22 Apr 2021 and is solely responsible for the information contained herein. Distributed by PUBT, unedited and unaltered, on 22 Apr 2021 10:02:25 UTC. \par \uc2 12,784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2021\par \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Filings\par \uc2 SAEXC\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021. As included in the Information \par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/0001829126-21-002782-index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Original document}}}\par \par \uc2 Primary Offering Prospectus (SEC Filing - 424B2)\par \par \uc2 The information in this preliminary pricing supplement is not complete and may be changed. This preliminary pricing supplement is not an offer to sell nor does it seek an offer to buy these securities in any jurisdiction where the offer or sale is not permitted.\par \par \uc2 Subject to completion dated April 21, 2021\par \par \uc2 \f2 Pricing supplementTo prospectus dated April 8, 2020,prospectus supplement dated April 8, 2020 andproduct supplement no. 2-II dated November 4, 2020 Registration Statement Nos. 333-236659 and 333-236659-01Dated April , 2021Rule 424(b)(2)\par JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC                                                                 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Structured\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investments\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 $\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Return Notes Linked to the Performance of an Equally Weighted Basket of Ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Relative to the U.S. Dollar due May 10, 2022\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fully and Unconditionally Guaranteed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 The notes are designed for investors who seek exposure to the performance of an equally weighted basket of ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar, as increased by the Basket Adjustment Factor, and who believe that the basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate relative to the U.S. dollar from the Pricing Date to the Observation Date. Assuming a Basket Adjustment Factor of 106.15%, due to the embedded cap on each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return of approximately 100% described below, the return on the notes at maturity is effectively capped at approximately 112.30%. \u183\'00\'B7 Investors should be willing to forgo interest payments and, assuming a Basket Adjustment Factor of 106.15%, if the Basket declines by more than approximately 5.79369%, be willing to lose some or all of their principal amount at maturity. \u183\'00\'B7 The notes are unsecured and unsubordinated obligations of JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC, which we refer to as \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Financial, the payment on which is fully and unconditionally guaranteed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Any payment on the notes is subject to the credit risk of JPMorgan Financial, as issuer of the notes, and the credit risk of \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as guarantor of the notes. \u183\'00\'B7 Minimum denominations of $10,000 and integral multiples of $1,000 in excess thereof\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Key Terms\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Issuer:                 JPMorgan Chase Financial Company LLC, an indirect, wholly owned finance subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par Guarantor:              \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par Basket:                 An equally weighted basket of ten \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (each, a 'Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' and together, the 'Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ') that measures the performance of the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the U.S. dollar (the 'Base \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ') \par Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :   The following table sets forth the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Starting Spot Rate\u8224\'20\'20 and the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Weight for each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Starting Spot Rate\u8224\'20\'20\u8224\'20\'20 Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Weight Indian rupee (INR) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Indonesian rupiah (IDR) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Russian ruble (RUB) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Turkish lira (TRY) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Offshore Chinese renminbi (CNH) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Philippine peso (PHP) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Colombian peso (COP) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Brazilian real (BRL) \u8224\'20\'20 10% Singapore dollar (SGD) \u8224\'20\'20 10% New Taiwan dollar (TWD) \u8224\'20\'20 10%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8224\'20\'20 The Starting Spot Rate is expressed as a number of units of the applicable Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per one U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8224\'20\'20\u8224\'20\'20 The Starting Spot Rate of each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be provided in the pricing supplement and will be the Spot Rate of that Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the Pricing Date, determined as specified under 'Additional Key Terms - Spot Rate' below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment at Maturity:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment at maturity will reflect the performance of the Basket, subject to the Basket Adjustment Factor. Accordingly, at maturity, you will receive an amount per $1,000 principal amount note calculated as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 $1,000 \u215\'00\'D7 (1 + Basket Return) \u215\'00\'D7 Basket Adjustment Factor\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In no event, however, will the payment at maturity be less than $0.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Assuming a Basket Adjustment Factor of 106.15%, you will lose some or all of your principal amount at maturity if the Basket Return reflects a decline in the closing level of the Basket of more than approximately 5.79369%. For more information on how the Basket Adjustment Factor can impact your payment at maturity, please see 'What Is the Total Return on the Notes at Maturity, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Basket?' in this pricing supplement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return formula used to calculate the Basket Return effectively limits the contribution of each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to an approximately 100% return but does not limit any negative contribution of any Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Accordingly, assuming a Basket Adjustment Factor of 106.15%, due to the embedded cap on each Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return, the return on the notes at maturity is effectively capped at approximately 112.30%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See 'Additional Key Terms - Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return,' 'How Does the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Return Formula Work?', 'Selected Risk Considerations - Risks Relating to the Notes Generally - Your Notes Are Subject to an Embedded Maximum Payment at Maturity' and 'What Is the Basket Return, Assuming a Range of Performances for the Reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?' in this pricing supplement for more information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basket Adjustment Factor: At least 106.15%. The actual Basket Adjustment Factor will be provided in the pricing supplement and will not be less than 106.15%. Pricing Date: On or about April 22, 2021 Original Issue Date: On or about April 27, 2021 (Settlement Date) Observation Date*: May 5, 2022 Maturity Date*: May 10, 2022 CUSIP: 48130UVX0 * Subject to postponement in the event of certain market disruption events and as described under 'General Terms of Notes - Postponement of a Determination Date - Notes Linked to Multiple Underlyings' and 'General Terms of Notes - Postponement of a Payment Date' in the accompanying product supplement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investing in the notes involves a number of risks. See 'Risk Factors' beginning on page S-2 of the accompanying prospectus supplement, 'Risk Factors' beginning on page PS-11 of the accompanying product supplement and 'Selected Risk Considerations' beginning on page PS-9 of this pricing supplement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Neither the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Securities and Exchange Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the 'SEC') nor any state securities commission has approved or disapproved of the notes or passed upon the accuracy or the adequacy of this pricing supplement or the accompanying product supplement, prospectus supplement and prospectus. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2            Price to Public(1)   Fees and Commissions (2)   Proceeds to Issuer \par Per note   $1,000               $                          $ \par Total      $                    $                          $ \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1) See 'Supplemental Use of Proceeds' in this pricing supplement for information about 