\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-U.S. may label Taiwan a  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  manipulator, says cenbank gov\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 05:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Taiwan meets three criteria to be labelled manipulator\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Taiwan c.bank\uc2  does not expect punitive measures\par \par \uc2 * C.bank sees economy staging "v-shaped" recovery in 2021 (Adds further comment on economic recovery)\par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, March 11 (Reuters) - Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Yang Chin-long said on Thursday that the United States may label the island a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator as it has already met Washington's three main criteria for making such a decision.\par \par \uc2 Yang, answering lawmaker questions in parliament, added that if this happens it would not be too serious and that there would be no immediate disadvantage for Taiwan and they did not expect to be subject to so-called "Section 301" measures that might lead to tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Yang said it's important to communicate with the United States about the reasons for Taiwan's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the U.S. quantitative easing policy and the effects of the China-U.S. trade war, which have boosted exports of Taiwan tech and expanded its trade surplus with the United States.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar's 5.6% gain against the greenback last year was among the strongest in Asia and it has continued to rise this year on the back of booming exports and a rebounding economy, though Yang saw signs for optimism.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar has recently been strong, and the Taiwan dollar exchange rate has been close to equilibrium. This is a good phenomenon," he said.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Wednesday a large spike in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spending last year, possibly putting the trade-dependent island in Washington's crosshairs to be labelled a manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan has now reached three of the criteria Washington uses to label a country a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, including how much it spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's trade surplus with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit $29.9 billion in 2020, according to official data, almost $7 billion more than in 2019, while the current account surplus last year was around 11% of GDP. Both exceed by a wide margin Washington's criteria for labelling a country a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's tech-focused economy has benefited from global demand for laptops, tablets and other equipment to support the work-from-home boom during the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Yang said he foresaw a "V-shaped" recovery for the economy this year, and that they would likely revise up their growth forecast at next week's quarterly meeting. (Reporting by Liang-sa Loh; Writing by Ben Blanchard; Editing by Christian Schmollinger & Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-11T05:38:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210311eh3b00cf9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
