\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Switzerland challenges US and will continue to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in the  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market despite threats\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) will maintain its ultra-expansion monetary policy, with negative interest rates and periodic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the franc (refugee asset) from appreciated. This decision comes after the direct indictment of the \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  to the small European country: "Switzerland is a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator."\par \par \uc2 This is not new to the SNB. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the franc from being overappreciating. A strong franc would jeopardize the Alpine country's exports, as it would 'make the goods and services produced in Switzerland and then sold abroad'. The Swiss franc is exchanged today for $1.13, while in 2019 both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were worth the same (parity).\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc is against the dollar in recent times A practical example: the more the franc appreciates, the more dollars an American company wants to buy Swiss watches to sell in the US is appreciated. Therefore, the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling francs (increases supply) and buying other foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ensuring a stable exchange rate while increasing international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance sheet.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's monetary policy is at the forefront of developed countries. At this last meeting, the SNB has kept the world's lowest nominal interest rates stable (-0.75%) and willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  has described the Alpine country as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. The \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  has also accused Vietnam of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in the same ad accusing Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 The SNB follows its own business "The coronavirus pandemic continues to have a strong adverse effect on the economy. In this difficult context, the SNB maintains its expansive monetary policy in order to stabilize economic activity and price developments," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says in its statement.\par \par \uc2 The agency kept its reference rate at -0.75%, such. It also maintained the interest rate it charges commercial banks for some deposits at -0.75%. Negative rates are one of the tools used by the SNB to relieve the bullish pressure of the Swiss franc as a shelter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grow on the SNB balance sheet When turbulence reaches markets, investors seek refuge in Swiss assets, leading to strong upward pressure for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A lot of 'scary' money from around the world is trying to get into Swiss assets, triggering demand for francs and their 'price', which is neither more nor less than the exchange rate.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the focus of the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 , which on Wednesday calledofficially to Switzerland as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 According to ING economists, Switzerland violates the three criteria established by the US to designate a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. In the four quarters to June 2020, Switzerland's bilateral trade surplus with the US amounted to $49 billion (the limit is $20 billion), its current account surplus was 8.8% of GDP (2% limit), and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was 14.2% of GDP. (2% U.S. limit).\par \par \uc2 The US indictment will not work However, Dutch bank experts believe that "this designation will have no impact on the monetary policy of the SNB in the coming years and will continue to implement its current policy. Indeed, given the level of inflation, it has no choice but to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the Swiss franc."\par \par \uc2 "If the US accusatory report raised doubts among investors about the will of the SNB and therefore leads to a strengthening of the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we believe that the SNB would have no choice but to further reinforce its message and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. In the end, this report could complicate the SNB's task a little if it creates uncertainty, but it will probably have no impact on monetary policy and Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Dutch bank experts say.\par \par \uc2 commentsforum1WhatsApp Facebook Twitter Linkedin\par \par \uc2 Dokum