\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan says hopes to cut trade surplus after U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  move\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par 07:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI (Reuters) -Taiwan hopes to cut its trade surplus with the United States to address U.S. concerns about the Taiwan dollar's exchange rate, the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The comments come after the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  on Wednesday added Taiwan to a "monitoring list" of countries whose \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices have caused concern, the first time the island has appeared on the list since 2017.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at parliament, Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Yen Tzung-ta said maintaining the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate was their obligation and priority, and that the U.S. decision was based on information for last year rather than the current exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's decision is a reflection of the international economic situation and the island's trade surplus with the United States, he added.\par \par \uc2 "We hope to cut the trade surplus with the United States," Yen said. "This is the long-term solution."\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's 2019 trade surplus with the United States hit $23 billion. The economy has benefited this year from global demand for Taiwan's high-tech goods from people forced to work and study at home during the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to stress to the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  that the benchmarks they use are disputed, Yen added.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan, however, will "do its best" to avoid being named a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator next year, he said.\par \par \uc2 Countries must at least have a $20 billion-plus bilateral trade surplus with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeding 2% of gross domestic product and a global current account surplus exceeding 2% of GDP to be labelled a manipulator, according to \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  criteria.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar has strengthened 7% against the U.S. dollar this year, and jumped more than 1% on Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan was last formally labelled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator by the United States in December 1992, but was later put on the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  monitoring list in 2016 and 2017.\par \par \uc2 The issue is particularly sensitive for Taiwan as the government is keen to keep in Washington's good books, with the United States being the Chinese-claimed island's most important international backer and arms seller.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Liang-sa Loh, Writing by Ben Blanchard; Editing by Himani Sarkar and Ana Nicolaci da Costa) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-17T06:10:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201217egch00b41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
