\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  manipulator tag for Switzerland unlikely to deter  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  approach\b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2020\par 18:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout with confirmation of manipulation tag, updated quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee, John Revill and David Lawder\par \par \uc2 LONDON/ZURICH/WASHINGTON, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Being named a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  may be an embarrassment for Switzerland, but the tag will likely have little effect on the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  on Wednesday labeled Switzerland and Vietnam as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators, saying they had both \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with at least part of Switzerland's action aimed at pushing down the Swiss franc to prevent effective balance of payments adjustments.\par \par \uc2 There would be no automatic punishment with a label, though U.S. law requires Washington to demand negotiations with designated countries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe subtle implication of being put on this list is that you eventually could come under sanctions, and that puts pressure on these countries not to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so much,\u8221\'20\'1D said Win Thin, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy at BBH, ahead of the report.\par \par \uc2 But he said that in Switzerland\u8217\'20\'19s case, as the exchange rate is its main tool for fighting deflation, "they may say, \u8216\'20\'18Well, tough\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is firmly under the Treasury's focus after spending 90 billion Swiss francs ($101.50 billion) on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first half of 2020 amid pandemic-driven safe-haven inflows.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has long argued it is not trying to weaken the franc to gain a trade advantage. Instead, it aims only to stem the appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to head off the threat of deflation, which runs contrary to its goal of price stability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSwitzerland has always been treated as a special case when it comes to exchange-rate policy and even the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  has conceded in the past that Switzerland\u8217\'20\'19s economic situation is 'distinctive' and that its monetary policy options are limited by its small stock of domestic assets,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Oxley, a senior European economist at Capital Economics, ahead of the report.\par \par \uc2 Latest data shows the SNB has dialed back on its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the franc is considered among the most over-valued major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world, according to various trade-weighted indexes.\par \par \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  staff estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/ESR/Issues/2020/07/28/2020-external-sector-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/ESR/Issues/2020/07/28/2020-external-sector-report}}}\uc2  in August that the franc was over-valued by 13.5% to 19.7% during 2019.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc jumped to a five-year high versus the U.S. dollar after the report was released. Analysts said it could, on balance, cause the Swiss franc to be more attractive.\par \par \uc2 Greg Anderson\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 BMO Capital Markets\uc2 , said that over the medium term "it's probably likely to lead to Swiss appreciation because they'll probably feel under the gun as a result of this finding and less likely and willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stifle franc strength."\par \par \uc2 The Treasury's three manipulation criteria are: a $20 billion-plus bilateral trade surplus with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeding 2% of GDP and a global current account surplus exceeding 2% of GDP.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland and Vietnam were the first to get the tag since China in 2019, at the height of U.S.-China trade tensions. That tag was removed in January as Washington and Beijing signed a trade agreement, citing a rebound in the yuan.\par \par \uc2 The SNB, which is to give its latest monetary policy decision on Thursday, said on Wednesday that it would not alter its monetary policy and remained willing to act aggressively on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 NOT BIDEN'S PROBLEM\par \par \uc2 The SNB's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remains central to its approach under Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SNB officials have long tried to explain their situation to Washington, noting that the franc rises because of global pressures. As a small, open economy, Switzerland can do little about that.\par \par \uc2 They will be hoping for a more sympathetic hearing under the incoming administration of President-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Switzerland being named as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  will not gather the same market attention under the new Biden administration as compared to a Trump one," said Kaspar Hense, a portfolio manager at BlueBay Asset Management in London, ahead of the report.\par \par \uc2 Michael Brown, senior analyst at payments firm Caxton, London, agreed, highlighting the upcoming changes to the U.S. administration and the SNB seeming set in its ways.\par \par \uc2 That confidence is also reflected in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Short term, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 's position tracker, which measures \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows on its trading platforms, shows hedge funds remain broadly bullish on the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 But medium term, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivative markets appear to be neutral about its prospects. Risk reversals, which show the ratio of calls to puts on the franc, show bets on further franc gains over three to six months broadly subdued.\par \par \uc2 BBH's Thin said any decision under the current U.S. administration may not matter. The new Treasury secretary "can come in and say \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t even believe in this,'\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 0.8867 Swiss francs)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by John Revill in Zurich, Saikat Chatterjee in London and David Lawder in Washington; Additional reporting by Andrea Shalal in Washington and Saqib Iqbal Ahmed, Sinead Carew and Ira Iosebashvili in New York; Editing by Megan Davies, Dan Grebler and Lisa Shumaker) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-16T18:00:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201216egcg0364d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
