\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Larry Fink, the inevitable partner of the country and the key to a final agreement\b0\par\par\uc2 1,564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Carlos Burgue\u241\'00\'F1o cburgueno@ambito.com.arThe Big Short is a 2015 film, where Hollywood explains in its style the 2008 "subprime" crisis; the only post-war financial event where Wall Street's financial system seriously came close to collapsing. The key to the film was to identify five cases where different fictional characters manage to anticipate stock market collapse and save their finances. One of those five cases is that of Jared Vennett, played by Ryan Gosling. He is a senior Wall Street executive, CEO of a very high-end investment fund; portrayed with all the common places of the occasion: superb, quite amoral and obviously a lover of greed, but who, in a moment of lucidity, accepts the advice of one of his financial advisers and sells on time all his mortgage insurance placements. Thus, he manages to get out of the crisis and position himself as a legend of the markets.\par \par \uc2 Vennett is a fictional character; but, over time, the film's writers acknowledged that it is a recreation of Larry Fink's role during the crisis. This, as CEO of BlackRock, was one of the few who managed to overcome 2008 growing in its assets and demonstrating a remarkable capacity for anticipation and reaction. Then, in his participation in post-crisis, Fink became the leading benchmark in the U.S. capital market, and managed to build the most important investment fund in history. It now handles an amount of money ($6 billion) that equals the GDP of Germany and the United States, and only is surpassed by the economies of the United States and China. It is so great that these same days, \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 's \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seriously considering limiting \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's advances in companies on the continent in crisis; via buying shares in quotes per floor.\par \par \uc2 This investment fund is the main benchmark of international creditors, with which the country must negotiate, and who accepted the role of the "bad police", to discuss a final agreement; as opposed to the other actors of this "Poker" that must be negotiated by the government, who assumed the position of "good cops", presenting offers closer to the failed Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n who won on May 8. However, all participants of this game know that the final destination of the negotiations (which must end yes or yes on July 30) will need the endorsement of the investment house of Fink and its main partners in this crusade (\uc2 Fidelity\uc2 , Ashmore and Pimco). In total, this group claims to represent together 25% of the total debt, so they hold the key of 75% necessary for the agreement to achieve the corresponding legality and close the possibility of a trial in the courts of New York.\par \par \uc2 As in almost every country in the world (including both hyperdeveloped states as countries such as Iraq or Afghanistan); \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  is a partner of Argentina; both in the financial economy and in the real economy. It is estimated to have restructured local debt of approximately $3 billion; of which almost us$2 billion corresponds to government titles issued under foreign legislation, and, as such, included in the ongoing renegotiation. Other $s1 billion are bonds released under local laws, especially the Treasury Bond (BOTE) 2023 and 2026, launched on May 14, 2018, with \uc2 Luis Caputo\uc2  as then new responsible for the rescue of the famous Lebac (in BCRA' desmer); an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the then "Messi" of the cabinet closed via telephone moving his personal contacts;placing the debt in the hands of \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  and Templeton. The intention of the Macri government was to hold the dollar around $25, dismantling the pressure of the pesos that would be released for the payment of the Leliq in exchange for a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper that would pay 20% a year and eventually beat inflation. It was even mentioned in those days that the arrival of these investors was due to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  government\uc2 , at a time when \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  and Donald Trump were economic and political allies worldwide. With the BOTE, both funds lost fortunes, which radically shifted \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's view of the country forward.\par \par \uc2 The world's largest fund also has an important presence as Argentina's partner in the real economy. Not only because of his \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a shareholder in multinationals with a strong local presence such as \uc2 Coca Cola\uc2 , \uc2 Bayer\uc2 , Apple, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , \uc2 Telef\u243\'00\'F3nica\uc2  or \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  (among many others); but for his shareholding as a shareholder of several of the most important companies in the capital market such as Mercado Libre, \uc2 Tenaris\uc2 , Grupo Galicia, \uc2 Banco Macro\uc2 , Telecom, \uc2 Pampa Energ\u237\'00\'EDa\uc2 , TGN, \uc2 Arcos Dorados\uc2  and \uc2 Adecoagro\uc2 . It is assumed that during the current crisis, several of these positions were sold, thus their participation may have declined. But where its most resonant is its local presence, it is like one of the fundamental private shareholders of the pearl of the Argentine state: \uc2 YPF\uc2 . The fund holds 9.77 million shares corresponding to 5.67% of the papers outstanding; a position in which during the international pandemic, as in the rest of its oil company holdings, he lost fortunes. At \uc2 YPF\uc2 , \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  is the second private investor after the Wellington mutual fund, and entered the oil company in the days when kirchnerism opened the capital to add international private partners, on the advice of \uc2 Repsol\uc2 's then good friends. Time passed, in April 2012 the oil company was renationalized, Spanish shareholders disappeared, but \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  held positions. It was even shown "friendly" with the country at the trial that the English vulture fund Burford initiated by the renationalization \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offering its "amicus curiae" services in the New York court of Loreta Preska where the case takes place.\par \par \uc2 Qualified in 2014 as "vulture fund" by \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de kirchner\uc2  (having shares in the Donneley trash can that closed its doors that year); Fink's fund's commitment as a local partner reached the top during the government of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 , with which he had two meetings and when he decided to open an office in July 2018 in the country, choosing two striking flats in the Catalinas area, from where he would monitor \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's huge possessions measured in billions of dollars in Argentina and Uruguay. At this point comes that interaction, that in this local headquarters, and under all possible security measures, there is an interconnection with the true key to \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's financial success; at least according to Fink's own vision.\par \par \uc2 In a room of these offices operates a terminal that operates online with the largest treasure of the investment fund: the Aladdin system. It is said on Wall Street, and the fund does not denies it, that it is the largest big data in the global financial system and one of the largest in \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in peer-to-peer competition with many of the security and recognition platforms of many of the central countries of the globe. Throughthis central trading system, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  can make virtual decisions about the financial movements of all the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the globe, calculating what was had, has or will have with a certain concrete investment or significant potential. Aladdin calculates the risk of a stock or a public title, advises buying and selling decisions, and evaluates future scenario. It takes into account not only the history of these roles, but who are the interested investors, managing to discern to the degree of speculation of the plaintiffs or bidders; in order to minimize the risk of each investment to the maximum. The system installed in East Wenatchee, Washington, was developed (and updated) in the largest of the secrets in Palo Alto, California and is the basis of decision-making for the incorporation or sale of assets from \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's other jewel, the iShares ETFs; the world's largest pension fund, and from where \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  manages the current or future retirements of millions of investors from all central countries (including mutuals) and which from 2009 to 2019 contributed an 80% profit. Fink himself explained this business, by making public his distrust of the survival of the welfare state according to the criteria of the second half of the twentieth century, based (on Aladdin's calculations) that the pyramid of contributions is blamed at such a speed that it will not be sustainable in time. What \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  offers is then a secure retirement, beyond the country where the contributor resides. The Aladdin system was connected to Buenos Aires several times in recent weeks; with the aim of realizing the carbon test of Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n's offer that he won on May 8. Obviously the conclusion was one of rejection. The important thing is that these results were distributed among all the booming bondholders, thus fueling the position of widespread rejection of the proposal that only garnered 18.6% support.\par \par \uc2 That's what it's all about when it comes to talking about Argentina playing a Poker match with the best Wall Street players; and that the match will only be won with professionalism. Guzman's offer must surpass the great big data of one of the largest players in the global financial market. So big that she was even the subject of a Hollywood film with a megastar as Ryan Reynolds as the lead.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200521eg5l002d3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
