\par\par \b \uc2 Ingredion Incorporated\uc2  Offer for \uc2 PureCircle Limited\b0\par\par\uc2 41,600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2020\par 15:07\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2020 \par \par \uc2 TIDMPURE\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 4132J\par \par \uc2 Ingredion Incorporated\par \par \uc2 09 April 2020\par \par \uc2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OR REGULATIONS OF SUCH JURISDICTION.\par \par \uc2 THIS ANNOUNCEMENT CONTAINS INSIDE INFORMATION.\par \par \uc2 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\par \par \uc2 9 April 2020\par \par \uc2 RECOMMENDED CASH ACQUISITION\par \par \uc2 of\par \par \uc2 PureCircle Limited\par \par \uc2 by\par \par \uc2 Ingredion SRSS Holdings Limited\par \par \uc2 a newly formed company wholly owned by \uc2 Ingredion Incorporated\par \par \uc2 to be effected by means of a scheme of arrangement\par \par \uc2 under section 99 of Bermuda Companies Act 1981\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 -- The board of directors of each of \uc2 PureCircle Limited\uc2  ("\uc2 PureCircle\uc2 ") and \uc2 Ingredion Incorporated\uc2  ("Ingredion") are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended acquisition whereby the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  will be acquired by Ingredion SRSS Holdings Limited ("Bidco") (a United Kingdom private limited company formed for the purposes of the Acquisition that is wholly owned by Ingredion) (the "Acquisition").\par \par \uc2 -- It is intended that the Acquisition will be implemented by means of a scheme of arrangement under the provisions of section 99 of the Bermuda Companies Act (or by way of a Takeover Offer under certain circumstances described in this announcement).\par \par \uc2 -- Under the terms of the Acquisition, \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  Shareholders will be entitled to receive 100 pence in cash for each \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  Share or eligible \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  Shareholders can elect to receive one Bidco Share in lieu of the full cash consideration, subject to scaling back and other terms as outlined in paragraph 12 below.\par \par \uc2 -- The Acquisition will be combined with an issue of new \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  Shares to Bidco immediately following the Acquisition becoming Effective, for the purpose of providing \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  with US$130 million of funding to allow it to repay, inter alia, the Outstanding \uc2 PureCircle\uc2  Debt (the "PureCircle Equity Injection"). Bidco will issue 261,643,939 new ordinary A shares of Bidco to Ingredion to enable Bidco to fund the PureCircle Equity Injection (the "Bidco Equity Injection"). The issue price of the new Bidco Shares is approximately US$0.4969 per Bidco Share, representing GBP0.4012 at an exchange rate of 1.2384 USD:GBP on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --          Upon completion of the Acquisition and the Bidco Equity Injection: \par    --           \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be wholly owned by Bidco; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bidco will be controlled by Ingredion, which will hold approximately 75 per cent. of the Bidco Shares in issue;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders electing for the Share Alternative described below will hold the remaining Bidco Shares as a minority investment, having been diluted from a holding of approximately 60 per cent. in Bidco to a holding of approximately 25 per cent. in Bidco; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --           the Bidco Shares will not be admitted to trading on any stock exchange; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bidco is expected to have repaid the Outstanding \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Debt, and to be in a net cash position; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Ingredion and the minority shareholders in Bidco will be parties to a Shareholders' Agreement that, among other things, will impose restrictions on transfers of Bidco Shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The UK City Code on Takeovers and Mergers (the "Takeover Code ") does not apply to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and although \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  has incorporated certain takeover-related provisions into the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bye-laws, these do not provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders with the full protections offered by the Takeover Code and enforcement of such provisions is the responsibility of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 , not the Panel. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Ingredion have agreed certain matters regarding the application of the Takeover Code to the Acquisition, and the terms of that agreement are summarised in this announcement. In particular, the attention of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders is drawn to the Conditions of Material Significance, which are set out in paragraphs 3 (k) to 3 (m) inclusive of Appendix I of this announcement. The effect of these Conditions of Material Significance is that, if any of them are not met, Bidco will be entitled to withdraw the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings from certain \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders and certain \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, together holding, in aggregate, 125,544,583 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing approximately 68.1 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 8 April 2020 (being the latest practicable date prior to the date of this announcement) containing irrevocable commitments to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept, or procure the acceptance of, the Takeover Offer. From the total irrevocable undertakings received, the Share Alternative has been elected with respect to 125,004,562 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing approximately 67.8 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement). As a result, this allows the remaining \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to elect for, at their sole option, either the Cash Offer or the Share Alternative (subject to pro rating of the Share Alternative).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cash Offer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Under the terms of the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will be entitled to receive: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    for each \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share:     100 pence in cash (the "Cash Offer") \par    --          The Cash Offer values the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately GBP185.3 million and represents an opportunity for \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to realise a cash sum for their \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by KPMG, consider the terms of the Cash Offer to be fair and reasonable. In providing advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, KPMG has taken into account the commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. KPMG is providing independent financial advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors for the purposes of the Cash Offer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share Alternative\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The proposed Acquisition also includes a Share Alternative under which eligible \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders can elect to receive: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    for each \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share:     1 Bidco Share (the "Share Alternative"), \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in lieu of the full cash consideration to which they would otherwise be entitled under the Acquisition (subject to scaling back in accordance with the terms of the Share Alternative) and subject to the terms and conditions of the Share Alternative detailed in paragraph 12 below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Bidco Shares will be independently valued and an estimate of the value of the Bidco Shares will be included in the Scheme Document. Further information about the Bidco Shares is set out in Appendix IV to this announcement and will also be included in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Share Alternative is not being made available to Restricted Overseas Shareholders, including \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders located or resident in the United States or who are otherwise US Persons, who shall receive cash pursuant to the Scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Only eligible \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who hold their \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares through a nominee account can elect for the Share Alternative in relation to part of their holding of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, on behalf of their respective nominees. There can be no partial elections for the Share Alternative with respect to the underlying nominee account of a single nominee.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- All other eligible \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will only be able to elect for the Share Alternative in relation to their entire holding of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares and not part only. To the extent that the elections for the Share Alternative cannot be satisfied in full, they will be scaled back pro rata to the size of such elections ( subject to any rounding adjustments as Ingredion, in its absolute discretion, considers practicable) and the balance of the consideration due to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who have made such elections will be satisfied in cash in accordance with the terms of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Under the Scheme, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who validly accept the Share Alternative will be issued up to 111,874,671 ordinary B shares in Bidco which will represent approximately 25 per cent. of the total number of Bidco Shares immediately after the Scheme becomes Effective and the Bidco Equity Injection completes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Bidco Shares will be unlisted, that is, not admitted to trading on any stock exchange, and will be subject to, among other things, restrictions on transfer. There are no plans to seek a public quotation on any recognised investment exchange or other public market for the Bidco Shares to be issued to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders under the Share Alternative. Further details on Bidco and the rights attaching to the Bidco Shares are set out in paragraphs 4 and 12 and Appendix IV to this announcement, and will also be included in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ingredion Incorporated\f28 \uc2 \f2  Offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Immediately after the Scheme becomes Effective, Bidco will issue 261,643,939 additional ordinary A shares to Ingredion for a total subscription price of US$130 million in connection with the Bidco Equity Injection thereby diluting the shareholding of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who validly accept the Share Alternative by approximately 59 per cent. This represents an issue price per new Bidco Share of $0.4969 equivalent to GBP0.4012 at an exchange rate of 1.2384 USD:GBP on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement). The proceeds of the Bidco Equity Injection will be used by Bidco to subscribe for additional shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  for a total subscription price of US$130 million pursuant to the PureCircle Equity Injection. The proceeds of the PureCircle Equity Injection will provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  with cash for general operating purposes and to repay the Outstanding \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Debt (approximately US$90 million as at the date of this announcement). Following the Bidco Equity Injection, Ingredion shall hold approximately 75 per cent. of the total number of Bidco Shares in issue, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who validly accept the Share Alternative holding the remainder. The effect of the Bidco Equity Injection will be that each \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholder who has elected for the Share Alternative will suffer an immediate dilution of their shareholding in Bidco of approximately 59 per cent. and the overall percentage of Bidco Shares which the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders hold in Bidco will decrease from approximately 60 per cent. to approximately 25 per cent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The ordinary A shares of Bidco, to be held by Ingredion, and the ordinary B shares in Bidco, to be held by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders electing for the Share Alternative, will have equal voting and dividend rights.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Subject to the Scheme becoming Effective, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not intend to pay any final or other dividend in respect of the financial year ended 30 June 2019 or the financial year ending 30 June 2020. The Cash Offer and the Share Alternative (as applicable) both assume that \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders will not receive a final dividend in respect of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's financial year ended 30 June 2019 or the financial year ending 30 June 2020. If on or after the date of this announcement and prior to the Effective Date, any dividend, distribution or other return of value is declared, made or paid by \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Cash Offer and the Share Alternative shall be reduced accordingly. In such circumstances, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders would be entitled to retain any such dividend, distribution or other return of value declared, made or paid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PureCircle Board Recommendation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cash Offer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, who have been so advised by KPMG as to the financial terms of the Cash Offer, consider the terms of the Cash Offer to be fair and reasonable. In providing their advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, KPMG has taken into account the commercial assessments of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors. KPMG is providing independent financial advice to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors for the purposes of the Cash Offer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Accordingly, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors intend to recommend unanimously that \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or, in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept or procure acceptance of the Takeover Offer), as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors (and their connected persons) who hold \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares have each irrevocably undertaken to do in respect of their own beneficial holdings of 820,021 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.4 per cent. of the share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share Alternative\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- In considering the terms of the Share Alternative, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors note that, while the Bidco Shares provide the option for a continued equity ownership in \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  with a much reduced debt level, the Bidco Shares will be unlisted and will represent a minority investment in a company controlled by Ingredion, following a material dilution of the relative holding of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who elect for the Share Alternative, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders who validly accept the Share Alternative holding approximately 25 per cent. of the Bidco Shares in issue, with Ingredion holding the remainder. The Bidco Shares will not be admitted to trading on any stock exchange or other public market and, with the exception of a number of mechanisms set out in the Shareholders' Agreement, will therefore be illiquid. As a result of the lack of a trading market for the Bidco Shares, their value will be uncertain and there may be more limited opportunities to sell the Bidco Shares other than the exit provisions agreed in the Shareholders' Agreement. Bidco has put in place a specific dividend policy which allows, subject to certain restrictions, for the distribution of a proportion of free cashflow to Bidco Shareholders. In addition, the Shareholders' Agreement amongst Ingredion and the minority shareholders in Bidco will impose significant restrictions on transfers of the Bidco Shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- For the reasons set out above, together with the risk factors and other investment considerations set out in paragraph 12 of this announcement, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors are not making any recommendation to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders as to whether or not they should elect for the Share Alternative. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors recommend that \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders do not elect for the Share Alternative unless they are fully cognisant of, and are prepared to accept, the risks and other investment considerations attaching to ownership of unlisted securities and have taken independent professional advice appropriate to their own financial circumstances and investment objectives.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders should ascertain whether acquiring or holding Bidco Shares is affected by the laws of the relevant jurisdiction in which they reside. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders should also consider whether Bidco Shares are a suitable investment in light of their own personal circumstances. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders are, therefore, strongly recommended to seek their own independent financial, tax and legal advice in light of their own particular circumstances and investment objectives before deciding whether to elect for the Share Alternative. Any decision to elect for the Share Alternative should be based on independent financial, tax and legal advice and full consideration of this announcement and the Scheme Document (when published).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Irrevocable Undertakings\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bidco has received irrevocable undertakings from certain \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders and from certain \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors, together holding, in aggregate, 125,544,583 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing approximately 68.1 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  containing irrevocable commitments to vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept, or procure the acceptance of, the Takeover Offer). From the total irrevocable undertakings received, the Share Alternative has been elected with respect to 125,004,562 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing approximately 67.8 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  in issue on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement) . As a result, this allows the remaining \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to elect for, at their sole option, either the Cash Offer or the Share Alternative (subject to pro rating of the Share Alternative).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Pursuant to the irrevocable undertakings referred to above, Olivier Maes and Guy Wollaert, have each irrevocably undertaken to vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept, or procure the acceptance of, the Takeover Offer) and to elect, at their option, for either the Cash Offer or the Share Alternative, in each case, in respect of their individual holdings of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, being 540,021 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.3 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued share capital on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- In addition, Peter Lai, has irrevocably undertaken to vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept, or procure the acceptance of, the Takeover Offer) and to elect to receive the Share Alternative (and not elect for the Cash Offer), in respect of his holding of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, being 280,000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.2 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued share capital on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ingredion Incorporated\f28 \uc2 \f2  Offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  -3-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Asian Investment Management Services Limited, Magomet Malsagov, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OLAM International Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Halfmoon Bay Capital, Wang Tak Company Ltd., Tan Boon Seng and the Alwaha Fund Limited (an investment vehicle of Wan Azmi Wan Hamzah, Tan Sri) have each irrevocably undertaken to vote (or procure the voting) in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the resolutions to be proposed at the General Meeting (or in the event that the Acquisition is implemented by way of a Takeover Offer, to accept, or procure the acceptance of, the Takeover Offer) and to elect for the Share Alternative (and not elect for the Cash Offer), in each case, in respect of all of their respective holdings of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares, being 124,724,562 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares representing, in aggregate, approximately 67.6 per cent. of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's issued share capital on 8 April 2020 (being the last Business Day before the date of this announcement).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- In the event that the elections for the Share Alternative would require more than 111,874,671 Bidco Shares to be issued then such elections would be scaled back pro rata to the size of such elections ( subject to any rounding adjustments as Ingredion, in its absolute discretion, considers practicable).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- As part of its proposal to the PureCircle Board, Ingredion placed an upper limit on the amount of cash it was willing to invest as part of the Acquisition and Bidco Equity Injection, combined with a required level of ongoing equity ownership in Bidco, and therefore held discussions with a number of the larger \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to ask them to elect for the Share Alternative. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders providing irrevocable undertakings to elect for the Share Alternative have done so in the knowledge that this provides all other \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders with the ability to choose either to accept the Cash Offer for their entire holding, or to elect for the Share Alternative on exactly the same terms (including in relation to pro rating) as those \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders providing irrevocable undertakings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Given that the Share Alternative is limited to a maximum of 111,874,671 Bidco Shares, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders and Directors who have irrevocably undertaken to elect to receive the Share Alternative (totalling 125,004,562 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares) will be subject to pro rating and will receive a mix of cash and Bidco Shares under the Acquisition, with the split dependant on the level of elections from other \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders for the Share Alternative.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Further details of these irrevocable undertakings are set out in Appendix III to this announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information on Bidco and Ingredion\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Bidco is a newly incorporated company registered in England and Wales which was formed for the purposes of the Acquisition. Bidco is wholly owned by Ingredion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Ingredion is headquartered in the Chicago, Illinois metropolitan area and is a leading global ingredient solutions provider serving customers in more than 120 countries. With annual net sales of greater than $6 billion for the year ended 31 December 2019, Ingredion turns grains, fruits, vegetables and other plant-based materials into value-added ingredient solutions for the food, beverage, animal, nutrition, brewing and industrial markets. Ingredion employs approximately 11,000 people and has a market capitalisation of over $5 billion. Ingredion's common stock is listed on the New York Stock Exchange.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Founded in 2002, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  was admitted to AIM on 11 December 2007, and to the Main Market on 28 October 2015. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  has offices in Europe, Asia and other locations globally. It is a leading producer and innovator of stevia sweeteners for the global food and beverage industry. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  collaborates with farmers who grow the stevia plants and with food beverage companies which seek to improve their low-and no-calorie formulations using a sweetener from plants. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  combines advanced research and development with full vertical integration from farm to high-quality, great tasting innovative stevia sweeteners. It has been granted over 214 stevia-related patents with more than 300 applied for patents pending.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  generated revenue of approximately US$124.0 million, gross profit of US$1.2 million and a loss before tax of US$72.2 million for the financial year ended 30 June 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 , earlier today released its unaudited interim results for the six month period ended 31 December 2019. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  generated revenue of approximately US$46.8 million, gross profit of US$10.7 million and loss before taxation of US$13.8 million for the six month period. Adjusted EBITDA for the period was US$(3.1) million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Conditions and Timetable\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- It is intended that the Acquisition will be implemented by way of a court-sanctioned scheme of arrangement under section 99 of the Bermuda Companies Act. However, Bidco reserves the right to elect to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer, subject to the terms of the Implementation Agreement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Implementation of the Scheme will be subject, among other conditions the approval of the requisite majority, respectively, of Voting Scheme Shareholders at the Court Meeting and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders at the General Meeting and to the sanction of the Court, at the Court Hearing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Scheme Document will contain further information about the Acquisition, full details of the Scheme and the procedures to be followed by \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders to approve the Scheme. The Scheme Document, together with notices of the Court Meeting and the General Meeting and the form of election and forms of proxy, and an indicative timetable for implementation of the Scheme, are expected to be dispatched to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders and, for information purposes only, to participants with \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share Rights, within 28 days of this announcement (save as agreed between \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Ingredion).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Completion of the Acquisition is conditional, amongst other things, on the following matters:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- passing of resolutions at the General Meeting (including approval of the PureCircle Equity Injection and amendments to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bye-laws to ensure that any \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares issued between approval of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Acquisition becoming Effective will be subject to the Scheme and that any \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares issued after the Acquisition becomes Effective will automatically be acquired by Bidco (or as it may direct) in exchange for the same cash price per \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Share as is due in respect of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shares acquired by Bidco under the Scheme);\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- a majority in number representing three-fourths (in value) in each class of members present and voting either in person or by proxy at a meeting sanctioned by the Court votes in favour of the Scheme;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- subsequent to the above voting threshold being attained, the Court making an order sanctioning the Scheme;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the resolutions required to implement the Scheme being duly passed by Voting Scheme Shareholders representing at least 75 per. cent of votes cast at the General Meeting;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the necessary compliance with the procedural requirements, if any, of the Bermuda Companies Act in relation to any reduction of the issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  associated with the cancellation of the Scheme Shares; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- a copy of the Order from the Court sanctioning the Scheme being delivered to the Registrar of Companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Conditions of Material Significance are specifically drawn to the attention of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders. The effect of the each Condition of Material Significance is that Bidco may be entitled to withdraw the offer if:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- except as Disclosed (which excludes \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 1H FY20 Interim Results), Bidco becomes aware that the PureCircle Group, was not, on the date of this announcement, or, if it thereafter ceases to be, the owner, free of Encumbrances (save for those Encumbrances created in the ordinary course of business or pursuant to third party financing documents that were Disclosed prior to the Announcement) of its material Supply Assets in China and/or in Malaysia and/or of its material registered patent assets;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- a UK regulatory authority has imposed, or announced or confirmed in writing that it will impose, a fine, or other financial penalty, on any member(s) of the PureCircle Group in an amount of more than an amount which \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Bidco have agreed is material (individually and/or in aggregate), in connection with the matters relating to the classification and valuation of inventory and/or \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2 's accounting records, as referred to in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Update Announcements; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- during the six month period which commenced on 1 January 2020, the PureCircle Group shall (in its internal monthly accounting records produced in a manner consistent with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  accounts for the financial year ended 30 June 2019) have recorded revenue of less than US$40 million, subject to certain exceptions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- If the Scheme does not become Effective by the Long Stop Date, the proposals will lapse except where the approval of Voting Scheme Shareholders at the Court Meeting and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders at the General Meeting is obtained before this date, in which case the Long Stop Date for the proposals may be extended to such later date as \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Ingredion may agree and, if appropriate, the Court may approve.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ingredion Incorporated\f28 \uc2 \f2  Offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  -4-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The global COVID-19 pandemic is restricting the ability of Governmental Entities around the world to conduct their normal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Bidco Directors expect that Governmental Entities will not be operating according to their normal schedules during the upcoming period and it may therefore take longer for the Conditions to be satisfied and the Court Meeting and/or General Meeting to be held. Accordingly, any dates in respect of the expected timetable for the Acquisition set out in this announcement are indicative, subject to change (by agreement between Bidco and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and, the Court, where required) and are provided by way of guidance only. Bidco shall keep the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  Shareholders notified of any updates or changes to the expected timetable as additional guidance is released. Further details regarding the expected timetable will be contained in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, Ingredion's president and chief executive officer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jim Zallie\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  advances our specialties strategy for sugar reduction and specialty sweeteners, by aligning with one of the most important food and beverage trends shaping the industry and impacting our customers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  is an industry-recognized innovator with a proven track record for producing great-tasting, naturally-based stevia ingredients. By combining our capabilities in product formulation, along with our experienced sales team, we will expand and complement our portfolio of stevia solutions to a growing and broader customer base.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We admire the business that \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  has built for nearly two decades and are excited to welcome them to the Ingredion family. We are ready to support this new phase of growth that is on-trend with consumers' desire for sustainable alternatives that are good for them, their families and the environment."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, Peter Lai, CEO of PureCircle, said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Ingredion is a leading global ingredient solutions provider serving over 18,000 customers in more than 120 countries. This acquisition will provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  with significant opportunities to increase our market penetration and grow our market share within the global stevia market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By leveraging Ingredion's global client base we will be able to take our great-tasting, high quality, non-GMO stevia ingredients to a larger, more diverse client base. In addition to the commercial benefits, the acquisition presents opportunities for increased operating efficiency through synergies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offer gives our shareholders an opportunity for the certainty of cash today, or the option to remain invested in \f28 \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  going forwards."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This summary should be read in conjunction with, and is subject to, the full text of this announcement (including its Appendices). The Acquisition will be subject to the Conditions and further terms set out in Appendix I to this announcement and to the full terms and conditions which shall be set out in the Scheme Document. Appendix II to this announcement contains the sources of information and bases for calculations of certain information contained in this announcement, Appendix III contains a summary of the irrevocable undertakings received in relation to the Acquisition, Appendix IV contains details on the Bidco Group and the Bidco Shares and Appendix V contains definitions of certain expressions used in this summary and in this announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Enquiries: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PureCircle\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  Peter Lai, CEO                            +60 3-2166 2206 \par  Jimmy Lim, CFO \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bidco \par  James Gray\f28 \uc2 \f2                                 +1 708 551 2574 \par  \par  Citi (Financial Adviser to Bidco \par   and In