\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Closing of the markets: Lisbon Falls and countergoes Europe. Interest below 0.5% for seven sessions\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Europe remained optimistic in the last session of the week, with only the Iberian squares being highlighted by the negative. In parallel, the interest of the Portuguese debt remains below 0.5%. The markets in Numbers\par \par \uc2 PSI-20 dropped 0.76% to 5,141.38 points\par \par \uc2 Stoxx 600 rose 0.33% to 390.80 points\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 devalues 0.50% to 3,018.73 points\par \par \uc2 Interest of the Portuguese debt to ten years aggravated 1.3 basis points for the 0.433%\par \par \uc2 Euro backs 0.24% to 1.1120 dollars\par \par \uc2 Oil in London breaks 0.32% to 63.19 dollars per barrel\par \par \uc2 Iberian Peninsula contrasts with Europe's green\par \par \uc2 The European scholarships closed mostly with a "positive note", and the aggregator of the 600 largest quoted, the Stoxx600, closed with a rise of 0.33% for the 390.80 points. The Iberian squares, Portugal and Madrid, were the exception.\par \par \uc2 Outside, investors maintain optimism, despite the fact that negative economic data have been disclosed in Germany, fueling the expectation that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  advances with a cut in interest to stimulate the economy of the old continent.Neighbouring Spain followed in disalignment with the upward trend of European peers on the day when the political impasse in the country is confirmed: Spain will continue without a government in full function, after parliament has voted against the investiture of the leader Socialist Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchezAs Prime Minister. In September there may be a new investiture session, but if the political blockade persists Spain advances to the fourth general elections in less than four years.\par \par \uc2 Already in Lisbon, the national scholarship gave 0.76% to 5,141.38 points, feeling the negative weight of the actions of BCP. The institution sank more than 5%, on the eve of the bank presenting the results of the semester.\u160\'00\'A0\par \par \uc2 Portuguese interest rates below 0.5% for seven sessions\par \par \uc2 The interest of the Portuguese debt to ten years closed with a worsening of 1.3 basis points for the 0.433%. However, this rise is not enough to return to the 0.5%, below which interest has been found for seven sessions. In Germany the trend was the opposite, with the remuneration rate of bonds with the same maturity to fall 1.5 basis points for the negative 0.379. The prize for the Portuguese debt against the German is thus placed in the 54 base points.\par \par \uc2 White House helps the dollar\par \par \uc2 The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  backs 0.24% to 1.1120 dollars in the first session after the White House adviser, Larry Kudlow, said in an interview with CNBC that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Oil loses ground with dollar appreciation\par \par \uc2 Oil prices are low in the main international markets, pushed by the appreciation of the dollar, which reduces the attractiveness of the assets denominated in the green note, as is the case of "black gold". The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strengthening after Larry Kudlow, the White House's economic adviser, has told CNBC that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ruling out any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bloomberg index for the dollar shot immediately to the highest level and over a month.\par \par \uc2 The West Texas Intermediate (WTI), reference crude for the U.S. that is traded in New York, continues to yield 0.30% to 55.85 dollars per barrel. In the London market, Brent of the North Sea backs 0.32% to 63.19 dollars.\par \par \uc2 Silver counts third week inGreenThe precious metal follows in the last session of the week with a devaluation of 0.13% for the 16.39 dollars per ounce, after this Thursday has reached a maximum of more than one year, in the 16.65 dollars. In accumulating the last five days, the balance is positive at 1.51%. This was the third consecutive week of gains for silver, after the previous one totaled 6.44% and in the preceding it valued 1.47%.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190726ef7q004hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
