\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-U.S. Treasury says nine trade partners deserve scrutiny over  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  practices\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2019\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, May 29 (Reuters) - The Trump administration said on Tuesday that no major trading partner met its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation criteria but nine countries, including China, required close attention as Washington presses tariffs and negotiations to address trade deficits.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury Department, in a semi-annual report to Congress, said it reviewed the policies of an expanded set of 21 major U.S. trading partners and found that nine required close attention due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices.\par \par \uc2 Ireland, Italy, Malaysia, Singapore and Vietnam were new additions to the watch list, which also includes China, Germany, Japan and South Korea. India and Switzerland were removed from the list of countries under extra scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 "No major U.S. trading partner met the relevant 2015 legislative criteria for enhanced analysis" as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, the department said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury's three criteria for determining whether a country can be labeled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator previously were a significant trade surplus with the United States, a sizeable current account surplus and evidence of one-sided, persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report, usually released in April, was delayed this year and Treasury expanded its monitoring criteria to include not just America's 12 largest trading partners but any country with more than $40 billion in bilateral goods trade. It also lowered the current account surplus threshold from 3 percent of GDP to 2 percent, suggesting an expanded list of countries surveyed.\par \par \uc2 In its October 2018 report, Treasury did not label China or any other trading partner as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Then, against the backdrop of rising trade tensions with China, it said the yuan's appreciation would likely exacerbate the U.S. trade deficit but U.S. officials had found Beijing appeared to be doing little to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.\par \par \uc2 China hopes the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not conduct unilateral assessments of other countries' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, \uc2 China's foreign ministry\uc2  spokesman \uc2 Lu Kang\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Whether a country is manipulating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not determined by the United States," Lu said at a daily media briefing in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "Relevant multilateral organizations have long had authoritative assessments of countries exchange rates."\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government has never taken measures to deliberately devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the head of China's banking regulator said in a state media interview on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In response to the report, Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it does not manipulate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for export advantage, while Malaysia said its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are limited to ensuring an orderly market and avoiding excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has imposed tariffs on $200 billion worth of Chinese imports and begun the process of imposing tariffs on another $300 billion in Chinese goods.\par \par \uc2 Talks to end the trade dispute between the two countries collapsed earlier this month, with the two sides in a stalemate over U.S. demands that China change its policies to address a number of key U.S. grievances, including theft of intellectual property and subsidies for state enterprises.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury Department said Washington believes direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  has been limited in the past year.\par \par \uc2 "Treasury will continue its enhanced bilateral engagement with China regarding exchange rate issues, given that the RMB (yuan) has fallen against the dollar by 8 percent over the last year in the context of an extremely large and widening bilateral trade surplus," Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 China needs to aggressively address market-distorting forces, including subsidies and state-owned enterprises, the Treasury statement said. Improved economic fundamentals would support a stronger yuan and help reduce China\u8217\'20\'19s trade surplus with the United States, it said. (Reporting by David Alexander; Additional reporting by John Geddie and Aradhana Aravindan in SINGAPORE, A. Ananthalakshmi in MALAYSIA and Michael Martina in BEIJING; Editing by Andrea Ricci, Sonya Hepinstall & Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-29T09:00:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190528ef5s03v75\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
