\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Venezuela: How the richest country on the continent ended up ruined and in chaos.\b0\par\par\uc2 2,045 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Luis H. Ball explains how democratic socialism precedes socialism, hunger and exile. (Wenceslao Cruz) If you throw a frog into boiling water, it jumps and survives with minor burns. But if you cook it slowly, you will not notice it at the beginning and it will die in the end. That is a common proverb in Venezuela that describes how socialism has gradually consumed the nation.\par \par \uc2 In a webinar coordinated by Atlas Network, Luis Henrique Ball, Venezuelan businessman and director of PanAm Post, gave an account of how he began 50 years ago with the nationalization of oil, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other industries, and explained the current political context lives Venezuela. This note includes the full video - in English.\par \par \uc2 In 1965, Venezuelan oil exports represented 2/3 of the international trade in hydrocarbons. The nation had the lowest inflation in the world for 100 years. There was a steady annual growth of 5% per year and 67% of the nation was middle class, according to European standards.\par \par \uc2 Still in the early eighties, Venezuela had a per capita income greater than the sum of all other countries in the Andean area, including Chile.\par \par \uc2 Since EE. UU He left the gold standard, only the Swiss franc and the Venezuelan bolivar managed to prevent his \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from losing its value. It remained that way until 1973 when both the legislative and executive branches were under the power of a single party and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nationalized, until that time not only independent but with shares listed on the Caracas stock exchange.\par \par \uc2 Not only industries were nationalized. The commercialization of coffee and cocoa remained exclusively in the hands of the State, when Venezuela was still the third world producer of coffee and the fifth of cocoa.\par \par \uc2 Then the price controls began, including the cost of movie tickets and French champagne were under the control of the Government.\par \par \uc2 Under the administration of Carlos Andr\u233\'00\'E9s P\u233\'00\'E9rez, democratic socialism seized Venezuela under the slogan "Now we are free to create a new type of entrepreneur" through loans granted by the State.\par \par \uc2 P\u233\'00\'E9rez followed the famous phrase of Lenin when in 1924 he announced the "New Economic Plan" in the USSR. The state took the dominant heights "of the economy and announced the emergence of a new man who would allow socialism, by releasing their individual desires to be replaced by the collective.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the size of the government quadrupled, and, paradoxically, while the income of this grew, so did poverty.\par \par \uc2 Under the influence of Juan Pablo P\u233\'00\'E9rez Alfonzo, the Venezuelan diplomat responsible for the creation of the \uc2 Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  (\uc2 OPEC\uc2 ) and who said that oil was "the excrement of the devil", Venezuela deliberately and constantly renounced its participation in the global oil market.\par \par \uc2 For 1981, oil production decreased, suicidally, to one third of the 1971 figure, despite the fact that the country had large reserves. This policy was maintained during several governments of different parties - all democratic socialists.\par \par \uc2 Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez took advantage of the twenty years of failure and impoverishment that was generated by these policies to tryseize power by way of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\uc2  was trained by Cuba Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez himself acknowledged having been recruited as an infiltrator of "the revolution" (lease of Havana) by Alfredo Maneiro. At that time leader of a guerrilla party, outlawed, of Maoist ideology.\par \par \uc2 Maneiro recruited Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez as a mole when he was second lieutenant, fresh out of the military academy. Before Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez carried out a failed coup d'\u233\'00\'E9tat in 1992, he had already been a Cuban mole in the Venezuelan Army for more than 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez gradually gained power: in 3 stages The only election that Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez won cleanly was that of 1998.\par \par \uc2 Having not taken power by assault, Chavez had to act gradually before revealing his true intentions and seizing absolute power. For them he designed a strategy in 3 stages.\par \par \uc2 Stage 1: Change the Constitution to achieve reelection, until then prohibited, and take control of the Judiciary.\par \par \uc2 Stage 2: Get international support to eventually counter the US. For this he counted on the great luck that the price of a barrel of oil multiplied by 20 during its first 10 years. The price of oil went from $ 7 / bbl to $ 140 / bbl. This allowed Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez to buy support in what was called the "Petrodiplomacia", financing socialist parties throughout the Americas and Spain.\par \par \uc2 Russia also benefited from this, not because it was ideologically close to Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez, but because he was very interested in the 17 billion dollars in arms sales that they agreed with \uc2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stage 3: After almost 10 years in power, Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez, at last, proclaimed himself a communist and fervent Marxist-Leninist and began a huge campaign of stylizations and confiscations such as had never been seen in Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 The workers' unions were put under state control, the leaders who opposed these measures were imprisoned or forced into exile.\par \par \uc2 These stages could alert Mexicans, since their current president, \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2 , who has so far faithfully copied Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez, has also begun his term without facing the businessmen. It remains to be seen if, like Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez, that is leaving him for the third stage of the process.\par \par \uc2 Since 1999, GDP has contracted by 60%. And now, thanks to the economic setback caused by the chavism, milk consumption was reduced by 80% and chicken by 75%.\par \par \uc2 Venezuelans are helpless Unlike the Constitution of the United States, which has a second amendment that guarantees the right to bear arms and form a militia if the government exceeds its powers, in 2008, \uc2 Hugo Chavez\uc2  made sure that there would never be an uprising and stripped to the Venezuelans of their weapons, even from their homes.\par \par \uc2 Years later, with Maduro at the helm, to avoid frightening the population and deceiving the international community, drones were banned in public demonstrations and people taking photos from the rooftops are stopped, in order to prevent them from circulating in the media and social networks evidences of repression generated by Chavismo.\par \par \uc2 20,000 Cubans are containing a military uprising With unarmed civilians, the Army would be the next in line to get Maduro out of power. However, 20,000 Cubans loyal to the regime are in charge of the personal safety of Maduro and the military high command and monitor any member of the service and his family to avoid an uprising.\par \par \uc2 The Cuban staff rotates in groups going in and out of the country. Havana knows that if Maduro falls, those 20,000 Cubans could be lynched and massacred, because the Venezuelan people are angryand tired of the dictatorship. However, Cuba does not have the logistics to withdraw its agents and take them home safely. This is one of the obstacles to achieve the exit of Maduro. Cuba needs it there.\par \par \uc2 Juan Guaido\uc2  is the constitutional president Strength is the only way to keep Maduro in power. According to the Venezuelan Constitution, \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  is the legitimate president and has the power to call elections, while Maduro is a usurper. It is a mistake and a demonstration of ignorance when a medium refers to Guaid\u243\'00\'F3 as "self-proclaimed"\par \par \uc2 To win the last presidential election, in which 80% of Venezuelans refused to vote, Maduro declared illegal the participation of the real opposition and imprisoned his main rivals. His only opposition was a former Chavez minister.\par \par \uc2 Their elections were not recognized throughout Latin America, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the United States. That is why, starting on January 10, \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  took office as president, because before the power vacuum or usurpation, the Constitution of Venezuela establishes it. Currently, Guaid\u243\'00\'F3 is recognized by more than 50 countries, including the United States, as the legitimate president recognized the South American country. The man who four years before received, literally, a bullet in the back to confront the Government.\par \par \uc2 We are lucky that Obama is no longer president It was under the Obama administration, who along with Tom Shannon, Assistant Secretary of State for Political Affairs, had an idea of democracy that involved having endless conversations with Maduro, believing that it would become more docile if the United States made concessions with Cuba.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the Trump administration knows that they are a band of criminals, and that a dialogue only allows the Chavista dictatorship to remain in power.\par \par \uc2 The crisis of the Venezuelan refugees is reaching Syrian proportions So far, almost 15% of the Venezuelan population emigrated. 4,000,000 are exiled, of whom 1,000,000 are refugees in Colombia. As for the percentage, there are more Venezuelan exiles than Cubans.\par \par \uc2 According to the Brookings Institute, another 4,000,000 more Venezuelans could leave Venezuela this year, which would mean that this would be equal to or more serious than the worst African crisis, worse than Syria.\par \par \uc2 This situation is unique in the history of America and could become one of the worst human catastrophes, if Maduro remains in power.\par \par \uc2 Socialism is normalized through culture When reading The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  in 2008, \uc2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\uc2  was presented as the reincarnation of Jesus Christ, due to social programs.\par \par \uc2 Just like what is happening in the United States now, universities became socialist territories 50 years ago in Venezuela. From then on, these ideas became politically popular.\par \par \uc2 Comparing Venezuela with the Middle East is a nonsense Today, the Trump administration is providing incredible support for Venezuela to return freedom and democracy. Meanwhile, some libertarian experts in the US are focused on discouraging the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when compared with Iran and Iraq. They have no idea what is really happening in Venezuela or in the region.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela is the most pro-EE country. UU of the world, has no connection with Central America. In 1997, Bill Clinton visited South America and the only city where his security team walked freely was Caracas. There he was acclaimed by the crowds.\par \par \uc2 That is why there is no need to invade, a demonstration of strength is enough to get rid of Cuba intelligence that threatens the soldiersvenezolanos.\par \par \uc2 \u191\'00\'BFQue sigue?\par \par \uc2 Maduro se va. No va a durar m\u225\'00\'E1s de un a\u241\'00\'F1o. Es como un prisionero en el Palacio de Miraflores, no tiene libertad de movimiento. Es universalmente odiado. Ya no tiene control.\par \par \uc2 .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-widget-header \{ width: 100%; color: #ffffff; background: #008ec5; padding: 6px 0px 2px 6px; font-family: 'notosans', 'Arial', 'Helvetica', 'sans-serif'; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; margin-bottom: 5px; border-bottom: 3px solid #ddd; font-size:18px; text-transform: uppercase; background: #003a5b !important; border-color: #bbbbbb; margin-top: 20px;\}.TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-text \{font-family:inherit;color:black;padding:3px 0 0px;text-align:left;line-height:1.25;font-size:12px;\}.TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-text:hover \{color:#008ec5;\}.TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-source \{font-family:inherit;color:#999;padding:2px 0 0px;text-align:left;font-size:10px;\}/* Smartphones (portrait and landscape) ----------- */@media only screen and (min-width : 320px) and (max-width : 699px) \{.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-widget .ob-widget-items-container \{ width: 100%; float: left;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-dynamic-rec-container \{ max-width: 100%; width: 97%;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1 ul.ob-widget-items-container.ob-multi-row.ob-row-1 \{ padding-top: 0;\}.TF_1 span.ob-unit.ob-rec-image-container \{ width: 34%; float: left;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-widget .ob-dynamic-rec-container ~ .ob-dynamic-rec-container \{ margin: 0;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-text \{ padding: 0px 0 0px 2%; \} .OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-source \{ float: left; margin-left: 2%;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-widget \{ min-width: 320px;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-text \{ line-height: 1; font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0px;\}.TF_1 li.ob-dynamic-rec-container \{ margin-bottom: 2.5%!important;\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-source \{ font-size: 10px;max-width: 190px;\}\}.OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-widget .ob_what a, .OUTBRAIN .TF_1.ob-strip-layout .ob-rec-source \{ font-weight: normal;\} .TF_1.ob-widget .ob_what \{ margin-bottom: 17px;\}\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190310ef390005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
