\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China Aug  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves fall slightly more than expected to $3.11 trln\b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2018\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, analysts' reaction)\par \par \uc2 * China's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves holding up despite recent sharp yuan fall\par \par \uc2 * Aug reserves fall $8.23 bln vs expected drop of $6.95 bln\par \par \uc2 * Trade frictions, rising dollar index behind reserves fall -SAFE\par \par \uc2 * C.bank seen uncomfortable with further yuan losses\par \par \uc2 * But looming escalation in US trade war could test \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's resolve\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Sept 7 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell slightly more than expected in August as the dollar extended gains and Beijing took steps to stabilise its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of mounting trade tensions with the United States.\par \par \uc2 Reserves fell $8.23 billion in August to $3.11 trillion, compared with a rise of $5.82 billion in July, data from the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters had expected a drop of $6.95 billion to $3.111 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Trade frictions, geopolitical and economic uncertainties and valuation changes due to the rising dollar index all contributed to the decline in reserves, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The yuan weakened for the fifth straight month in August as the dollar remained buoyant, raising concerns that Beijing may be considering a stealth devaluation to support its exporters as the Sino-U.S. trade war heated up.\par \par \uc2 In August, the yuan fell nearly 0.2 percent against the dollar. The dollar index that measures it against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 0.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 But the yuan clawed back a bit of ground later in the month after a series of moves by \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled that it was not comfortable with further losses.\par \par \uc2 Julian Evans-Pritchard at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's reluctance to use its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to support the yuan showed it had leant a lesson from 2015-16, when its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to stem rapid falls in reserves.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales also leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  open to accusations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, even if it is acting to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  not weaken it," Evans-Pritchard said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Perhaps more importantly, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  appears to have fine-tuned the art of guiding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in less obvious ways, leaning on state banks to help offset private capital outflows and stabilise the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 has closed loopholes that could be used for capital flight, made it more expensive for speculators to bet against the yuan and re-activated a mysterious "counter-cyclical" factor in its daily official guidance rate calculations to reduce volatility.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to decide soon whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more forcefully to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  readies more sweeping tariffs on Chinese goods.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's administration could impose levies on $200 billion more of Chinese goods after a public comment period ended on Thursday, and the tariffs could go into effect soon afterward.\par \par \uc2 "The renminbi's recent depreciation will offset much of the (economic) impact of the tariffs proposed so far. But a further escalation of the trade conflict with the U.S. would clearly be a concern," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said in a note on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 CAPITAL CONTROLS A SOLID FIREWALL\par \par \uc2 Despite the yuan's steady depreciation in recent months, there have been few signs so far of a spike in capital outflows like those seen a few years ago after a surprise devaluation by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists polled by Reuters this week predict only a small gain for the yuan over the next 12 months as policymakers draw a line in the sand, but a significant minority believe authorities could let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken again if global trade conditions worsen.\par \par \uc2 Controls on capital flows that China imposed in 2016 and 2017 also seem to have helped prevent a recurrence of the volatility seen then, when Beijing unsuccessfully burned through a trillion dollars worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to try and contain the yuan's fall and stem capital flight.\par \par \uc2 The value of China's gold reserves fell to $71.228 billion at the end of August, from $72.324 billion at the end of July.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao and Cheng Fang; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-7T10:31:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180907ee970197t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
