\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Market closure: Relief in Turkey infects world markets\b0\par\par\uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Investors have eased the pressure on Turkey and this has been reflected across Europe. European stock markets ended without a definite trend, but interest rates dropped and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered. Markets in numbers\par \par \uc2 PSI-20 yielded 0.59% to 5,504.50 points\par \par \uc2 Stoxx 600 closed steady at 384.92 points\par \par \uc2 S & P 500 adds 0.58% to 2,838.17 points\par \par \uc2 Portugal's 10-year Yield shrinks 3 basis points to 1.817%\par \par \uc2 Euro depreciates 0.51% to $ 1.1352\par \par \uc2 Oil rises 1.05% to $ 73.37 a barrel in London\par \par \uc2 Mixed European stock markets on recovery day of the lira\par \par \uc2 In the last two sessions, European stock markets were heavily hit by turmoil in Turkey. The exposure of the quoted to the country, especially the banking sector, caused losses of 11 billion euros in two days. But this Tuesday, August 14, the stock markets calmed slightly. The Stoxx 600 index, which aggregates the top 600 European shares, remained broadly unchanged at 384.92 points. In the remaining European exchanges there were those who registered gains like Athens, Amsterdam and Frankfurt or losses like Milan, London or Paris.\par \par \uc2 In the case of the PSI-20, the national stock exchange was also penalized by the effect of Turkey on European exchanges, notably the BCP which fell more than 1%. In addition, Navigator - and \uc2 Semapa\uc2 , since it controls nearly 70% of Navigator - continued to devalue in the hangover of the news that it will have to pay a 37% rate for sales in the United States, unlike the 0% previously provided. The paper sector was one of those that dragged the PSI-20 further into negative territory, as did retailers such as Sonae and Jer\u243\'00\'F3nimo Martins.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's interest sank more than 100 points The last few days have been marked by steep rises in interest rates in Turkey as a result of the economic crisis intensifying in the country. On Tuesday, the mood subsided, with authorities pushing for more measures to try to stem the fall of the lira and heighten economic tensions. And some coolness came to light. The implied interest rate on Turkey's 10-year debt falls by 132 basis points to 21.37%. This context has influenced most markets. Europe's interest rates have also risen in recent days, and they have come back in this last session. The rate associated with Portuguese debt fell three points to 1.817%. In Italy the decline was even more pronounced: 7.2 points to 3.03%.\par \par \uc2 Euribor remains at 3, 6 and 12 months and rises to 9 months\par \par \uc2 The three-month Euribor, in negative figures since April 21, 2015, remained at -0.319%. In contrast, the six-month rate, the most used in Portugal in mortgage loans and which entered negative territory for the first time on November 6, 2015, remained at -0.266%. At nine months, Euribor rose 0.003 points to -0.207%, while within 12 months remained at -0.166%.\par \par \uc2 Turkish lira recovers and encourages exchange market\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira was able to recover in Tuesday's session after three consecutive sessions to mark historic lows due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inability to control inflation and as a result of worries surrounding the diplomatic war with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But today, with new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to recover and has already been valuing 7% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 This performance has boosted most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emerging markets, but this has noteuro, which continues to yield 0.51% to $ 1.1352 (the lowest since July 2017) at a time when volatility is maintained while driving in Turkey - which has said it will boycott US electronics, Americans, such as the iPhone - and in Italy.\par \par \uc2 Oil rises with relief in Turkey and prospects of stock drop\par \par \uc2 "Black gold" prices continue to trade bullish, sparked by turmoil in Turkey and the prospect of a further decline in US crude oil reserves last week.\par \par \uc2 The September contract of the West Texas Intermediate (WTI), traded in the New York market, continues to add 1.04% to $ 67.90. Meanwhile, the North Sea Brent futures contract prices - which are traded in London and serve as a reference for Portuguese imports - for September delivery continue to advance 1.05% to 73.37 dollars per barrel.\par \par \uc2 Industrial metals with generalized fragility\par \par \uc2 Base metals prices are in negative territory, not only due to the reversal of copper trend but also due to the continued poor performance of other congeners such as zinc, aluminum and nickel.\par \par \uc2 The supply of Chilean copper was experiencing disruption due to a strike at the Chilean mine at La Escondida, but an agreement was reached to stop this shutdown and the industrial metal returned to the falls.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180814ee8e0040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
