\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Trump does not try to control dollar value: \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not trying to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  on Saturday, and insisted that a strong dollar reflects a strong US economy and is something desirable for the North American country. long term.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin, who is in Buenos Aires for the meeting of finance ministers and heads of central banks of the G20, told reporters that both he and Trump fully support the independence of the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump, in a recent unprecedented event, criticized the strength of the dollar and the monetary policy of the Fed. The president wrote in his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account on Friday that increases in interest rates of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  take away competitiveness from exports Americans\par \par \uc2 "Let me be clear, this is by no means that the president is trying to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," Mnuchin said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not trying to control the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin said both he and Trump fully support the Fed's independence and that he has "enormous confidence" in the work that \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is doing as head of the entity.\par \par \uc2 The official said he could not explain why the US president made such comments about the direction of the Fed's interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "I just want to assure you that the intention was not to pressure the Fed or put its independence at risk," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin played down the fact that he will not have a formal bilateral meeting with Chinese officials at the G20 meeting, at a time of escalating tariff wars between the two largest economies in the world.\par \par \uc2 The secretary of the Treasury explained that his usual interlocutor, the official economic adviser of China Liu He, is not attending the event in Buenos Aires.\par \par \uc2 "If the right people were here, we would be meeting," Mnuchin told Reuters in an interview on Friday.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, he added that the Trump administration has been clear with the Chinese government on the steps that must be taken to remove tariffs that the United States applied on Chinese exports for 34,000 million dollars.\par \par \uc2 "Although the objective is to reduce the trade deficit, the idea of ??doing that is for them to open their markets so that we can compete in fair terms and we can increase exports," he explained.\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin said he has not yet seen a macroeconomic impact of tariffs imposed by the United States on steel, aluminum and Chinese goods, nor of the retaliatory measures taken by its trading partners.\par \par \uc2 But he said there have been microeconomic effects in some sectors and that the government was monitoring them closely and looking for ways to help American farmers who were affected by retaliatory tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180721ee7l004y1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
