\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  ease on rising trade tensions\b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2018\par 07:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * S.Korean won biggest loser in region\par     * Singapore dollar firms amid largely weak EM Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Christina Martin\par     April 3 - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped on Tuesday,\par as the dollar steadied against the yen after three straight\par sessions of declines on rising trade tensions between the United\par States and China.\par     China imposed extra tariffs on 128 U.S. products, in\par response to U.S. tariffs on imports of aluminium and steel,\par deepening a dispute between the world's two biggest economies\par and stoking concerns about the impact on global growth.\par     On Tuesday, China's ambassador to Washington said Beijing\par would take counter-measures of the "same proportion" and scale\par if the United States imposes further tariffs on Chinese goods\par from a trade probe, state television reported.\par     China's tit-for-tat tariffs hurt the dollar, although it saw\par some buying during early Asian trading on Tuesday. The dollar\par index was still a shade softer against a basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Wall Street shares plunged on Monday as investors fled\par technology stocks amid resurgent trade war worries, with key\par indexes trading below their 200-day moving averages and the S&P\par 500 closing below that pivotal technical level for the first\par time since June 2016. \par     "Asian equities opened in the red this morning, following\par the sell-off in U.S. equities overnight. Persistent price action\par below 200 DMA (day moving averages), trade war fears and UST\par yield curve compression could result in a self-inflicted\par risk-off cycle," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a Singapore-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with Maybank.\par     "It is a cautious start to the week for EM Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . We\par believe equity markets will be closely watched in the short term\par for cues on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  direction."\par     The South Korean won was the biggest loser among\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , down as much as 0.3 percent, after hitting its\par strongest intraday level since Oct. 2014 on Monday. \par     South Korea's government official in charge of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday that authorities will act to curb sharp\par fluctuations in the won if necessary.\par     The Thai baht and China's yuan both slid\par as much as 0.2 percent, while the Philippine peso inched\par down 0.1 percent.\par     Meanwhile, the Singapore dollar firmed as much as\par 0.2 percent, and the Indian rupee edged up 0.1 percent.\par     Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to tighten monetary\par policy in April for the first time in six years, with economic\par growth solid and the labour market showing signs of improvement,\par a Reuters poll of economists found. \par     \par     WON\par     The South Korean won, which hit a three-and-a-half-year high\par on Monday, weakened as much as 0.2 percent on Tuesday. \par     South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities said there is no change\par in their stance to take action in cases of high \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par volatility after the Korean won hit a 3-1/2-year high on Monday.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often presses Seoul to disclose details of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to improve transparency of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policies.\par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0455 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0455 GMT                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              105.950     105.88        -0.07\par  Sing dlr               1.310       1.3124        +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr             29.145      29.142        -0.01\par  Korean won             1058.600    1056.6        -0.19\par  Baht                   31.200      31.15         -0.16\par  Peso                   52.063      52.035        -0.05\par  Rupiah                 13765.000   13753         -0.09\par  Rupee                  65.095      65.17         +0.12\par  Ringgit                3.864       3.86          -0.10\par  Yuan                   6.288       6.2810        -0.11\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2018                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              105.950     112.67        +6.34\par  Sing dlr               1.310       1.3373        +2.06\par  Taiwan dlr             29.145      29.848        +2.41\par  Korean won             1058.600    1070.50       +1.12\par  Baht                   31.200      32.58      