\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-On a mission: \uc2 Taiwan  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief's bid to escape U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  glare\b0\par\par\uc2 947 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2017\par 01:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats item from Tuesday)               \par \par \uc2 * Taiwan on U.S. watchlist of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head wants Taiwan off the U.S. watchlist               \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get off watchlist               \par \par \uc2 * But U.S. keeps island on the list, demands "durable" change               \par \par \uc2 By Liang-Sa Loh and J.R. Wu               \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, May 16 (Reuters) - As he counts down his final months at the helm of \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Governor Perng Fai-nan has made it his mission to get Taiwan off the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 's list of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators by turning on its head a decades-old policy of keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak.               \par \par \uc2 The change is bearing some fruit, but Perng is in a race against time to completely remove Taiwan from the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 's list of countries being monitored for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation before he leaves office early next year.               \par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  has recognised Taiwan's efforts to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suppress the strength of the Taiwan dollar, it wants to make sure the change is longer lasting before taking the island off of its watchlist. Others on the U.S. watchlist include China and Germany.               \par \par \uc2 Under U.S. rules, economies with a hefty trade surplus with the United States, a current account surplus exceeding 3 percent of their GDP and which use heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be labelled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators and could be subject to punitive measures.               \par \par \uc2 The criteria, introduced in 2016, gave \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a roadmap to follow. Its trade surplus with the United States was below the U.S.' threshold, while its current account surplus as a small, trade-reliant economy, was well above the threshold at 13 percent of GDP.               \par \par \uc2 So the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's best hope to get off the watchlist was to ease up on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said.               \par \par \uc2 Now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees Taiwan heading in the right direction, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department suggested.               \par \par \uc2 "This time Taiwan only fulfilled one criteria," said Harry Yen, referring to the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's latest twice-yearly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator report in April.                              \par \par \uc2 DRAMATIC TURN               \par \par \uc2 The change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy marked a dramatic turn for a trading island that punches way above its economic weight.               \par \par \uc2 For nearly two decades, Perng's management of the exchange rate had been seen at home as a pillar of support for exporters, which fuel more than half the economy and are vital to many global technology supply chains.               \par \par \uc2 Over the years, Perng was a regular in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading room, barking orders to directly manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said. A fish tank was installed in the trading room, filled with cichlids that are known for being nimble and fast \u8211\'20\'13 something the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers wanted to emulate in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.               \par \par \uc2 "If changes in the market are very big, Perng will take command when he is in the trading room," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, who declined to be identified because of the sensitivity of the issue.               \par \par \uc2 Neither Perng nor his office wanted to comment for this story.               \par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight management, the Taiwan dollar fell 14 percent against the U.S. dollar between early 2011 and 2016.               \par \par \uc2 But since Perng changed policy, the Taiwan dollar has risen sharply. It is up 7 percent against the dollar this year alone, sitting alongside the Korean won as Asia's strongest major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The shift was rewarded by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 , which said in its October 2016 report that the \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had cut back on its "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of the trading day, which many market participants had viewed as a preference for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation."               \par \par \uc2 By April 2017, Treasury officials said Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen below red-line levels, so it no longer met the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  criterion, but they kept it on their watchlist because they were not convinced the change was long lasting.               \par \par \uc2 Taiwan can only be removed from the watchlist when it meets only one criterion for two consecutive Treasury reports.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  said Taiwan needs a "durable, not one-off" improvement to get off the watch list. Another potential delay could be a disagreement over how income on the island's $438 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves is calculated, Taiwan sources said. The Treasury sees the income as evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .                              \par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN FACTOR               \par \par \uc2 The change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has not come without its downside.               \par \par \uc2 The world's largest contract chipmaker \uc2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co\uc2  said last month that its first-quarter revenue fell short by T$6 billion ($200 million) due to the local dollar's strength.               \par \par \uc2 It said it expected the Taiwan dollar to keep rising, which in turn could hit its revenue because most of it is denominated in U.S. dollars.               \par \par \uc2 There is also an unknown factor Taiwan may have to contend with in trying to avoid the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator label \u8211\'20\'13 an unpredictable U.S. president.               \par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has toned down his rhetoric since entering office in January, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials fear Trump might push for a different way to declare big exporters a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.               \par \par \uc2 "For example, if the U.S. economy doesn't do well and America's trade deficit doesn't improve, the rumblings will get louder and to resolve domestic issues Trump could 'change the status quo' and Taiwan could stay on the monitoring list," another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.               \par \par \uc2 "This report is written by the United States, so it is not something Perng Fai-nan can control."               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-5-17T00:31:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170516ed5g00xev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
