\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan stocks fall slightly; U.S. keeps country on  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  monitoring list\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2017\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIPEI, April 17 (Reuters) - Taiwan stocks fell slightly on\par Monday, largely tracking regional shares and unnerved by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to keep Taiwan on a monitoring list for\par its trade practices.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week maintained that Taiwan's\par material current account surplus merited Taiwan to stay on its\par monitoring list, though it dropped a second criterion that\par Taiwan had met in October of one-sided \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.             \par     "Treasury urges Taiwan's authorities to demonstrate a\par durable shift to a policy of limiting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to only exceptional circumstances of disorderly\par market conditions," it warned.  \par     As of 0338 GMT, the main TAIEX index         was down 0.16\par percent at 9,717.28, after closing 1.1 percent lower in the\par previous session.\par     The electronics subindex         was 0.04 percent lower,\par while the financial subindex         was down 0.55 percent.  \par     Among actively traded stocks, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cathay Financial Holding\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par          , which is engaged mainly in the financing businesses,\par dipped 0.84 percent. \par     In response to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision, Harry Yen,\par director-general of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par department, told Reuters on Saturday that it may be difficult\par for Taiwan to fix its current account surplus. \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  estimated the amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par accounted for 1.8 percent of GDP; the other criterion is related\par to Taiwan's high savings rate, so there's no way to satisfy\par that," Yen said. \par     Nevertheless, focusing on a bright spot, analysts said\par Taiwan's efforts to let its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen paid off in the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to drop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  criteria, but cautioned the trend may not last.  \par     "From the beginning of this year, the Taiwan dollar has\par already strengthened quite a lot, but it likely won't go much\par further as the impact will be on our exports," said Tony Chen, a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taishin Financial Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     "In Q2, we might even see some depreciation," he added.     \par     \par     On Monday, the Taiwan dollar          strengthened T$0.082\par to stand at T$30.318 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par  (Reporting by Jess Macy Yu and Liang-sa Loh in TAIPEI; Editing\par by Subhranshu Sahu)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-4-17T05:13:28.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170417ed4h0058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
