\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS-Trump finds markets, too, are complicated beasts\b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2017\par 16:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist.  The opinions expressed are her own.)               \par \par \uc2 By Gina Chon               \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, April 13 (Reuters Breakingviews) - As with healthcare, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is finding that markets are complicated, too. The U.S. president no longer wants to label Beijing a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. He belatedly learned that the yuan hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been purposely devalued for a while. He's also warming to the dovish Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and the \uc2 Export-Import Bank\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 During his campaign, Trump repeatedly pledged to label China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator on \u8220\'20\'1Cday one\u8221\'20\'1D in office. He accused Beijing of purposely weakening the yuan to make Chinese exports more attractive. There are three conditions a country must meet to be labeled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, such as having a trade surplus with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and persistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.               \par \par \uc2 China had been trying to depress its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for years in the 2000s. However over the last two years, China has been the biggest net seller of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stem capital flight. Trump told the Wall Street Journal on Wednesday that China actually hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been manipulating the yuan for months.               \par \par \uc2 He also reversed course on his criticisms of Yellen, whom he said he'd like to replace during the campaign. He said he respects Yellen and given the strong U.S. dollar, he prefers interest rates to stay low. But that clashes with his economic goals. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects to raise rates more quickly this year because of the healthy economy and jobs growth.               \par \par \uc2 Trump also now supports Ex-Im, the government credit agency for foreign purchases of U.S. goods. He said it helps small businesses and other countries have similar lenders. The bank has been hobbled in its mission by conservative lawmakers, including Trump ally and House Financial Services Committee Chairman \uc2 Jeb Hensarling\uc2 , who accuse it of crony capitalism.               \par \par \uc2 As a real-estate mogul, Trump had limited experience with the stock market, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings and other market factors. He\u8217\'20\'19s being schooled by Wall Street pros like Blackstone boss Steve Schwarzman and former Goldman Sachs President \uc2 Gary Cohn\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s director of the National Economic Council.               \par \par \uc2 In February, during the failed effort to repeal Obamacare, Trump said \u8220\'20\'1Cnobody knew health care could be so complicated." His reversals on the yuan, Yellen and Ex-Im suggest he's coming to similar realizations on matters of import to markets. Even if the inconsistencies are worrisome, at least he seems to be learning on the job.               \par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GinaChon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/GinaChon}}}\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS               \par \par \uc2 - President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told the Wall Street Journal on April 12 that China hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been manipulating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for months and he also doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to jeopardize his relationship with Beijing, whose help he needs on combating the North Korea threat. The \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  will not label China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in its latest report on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices of major trade partners, which is due April 15. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, he repeatedly promised to impose the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -manipulator label on China on \u8220\'20\'1Cday one\u8221\'20\'1D in office.               \par \par \uc2 - Under the U.S. Trade Facilitation and Trade Enforcement Act of 2015, a country can be labeled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator if it meets three criteria. These include having a significant bilateral trade surplus with the United States, having a material current-account surplus, and engaging in persistent, one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. If a country is found to have met those conditions, Washington would start negotiations to reduce those practices. If there is no progress after one year, the United States could impose several penalties such as excluding the country from government procurement contracts and calling for heightened surveillance by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on               \par \par \uc2 - SIGN UP FOR BREAKINGVIEWS EMAIL ALERTS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe}}}\par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-4-13T15:49:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170413ed4d00hda\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
