report, said Derek Scissors, a resident scholar and China trade expert at the \uc2 American Enterprise Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I would be very surprised if a year from now the Obama criteria were still in place," Scissors said.\par \par \uc2 The most logical option would be to lengthen the time period for reviewing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 12 months to several years, capturing more past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by China, according to the policy experts.\par \par \uc2 One senior South Korean official told Reuters that doing this would likely lead to manipulator designations for South Korea, Taiwan and possibly other countries.\par \par \uc2 Treasury also could reduce the current account surplus threshold below 3 percent of GDP to try to capture more potential offenders, but that would be at odds with longstanding views of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  and G20 finance officials that 3 pct of GDP is about where surpluses start to become a concern.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Lawder; additional reporting by Christine Kim in Seoul; Editing by David Chance and Grant McCool) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-4-5T23:40:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170405ed4500whh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
