\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar jumps to three-week high ahead of U.S. jobs data\b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2016\par 21:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Friday's U.S. payroll data in focus for Fed rate hike view\par \par \uc2 * Fed's Fischer says job market near full strength (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Karen Brettell\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a three-week high against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a one-month high against the yen, on Tuesday as investors looked ahead to crucial jobs data this week for clues on when the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will next raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Hawkish comments on Friday by Fed Chair Janet Yellen and Vice Chair \uc2 Stanley Fischer\uc2  increased expectations the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hike at its September policy meeting, though most investors and economists view a single increase at the December meeting as more likely.\par \par \uc2 The next key indicator is Friday's jobs report for August, which is expected to show employers added 180,000 jobs in the month, according to the median estimate of 89 economists polled by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "We had a bit more hawkish tone from Yellen at Jackson Hole and that was reinforced by Fischer," said Mark McCormick, North American head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 "The market is refocusing itself on the upcoming data releases and I think that's helping a rethink of where the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's is going to be in the second half of the year," he said.\par \par \uc2 Friday's jobs data will be preceded on Wednesday by the ADP National Employment Report of private-sector payrolls.\par \par \uc2 Fischer, who said that the data could weigh on any rates decision, gave no fresh clues on timing in a television interview on Tuesday. He said the U.S. job market is nearly at full strength and the pace of Fed rate increases will depend on how well the economy is doing.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of six majors, rose as high as to 96.143, its highest level since Aug. 9, before falling back to 96.062, up 0.50 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 The greenback gained 1.1 percent against the yen to 103.01 , after earlier hitting 103.13, the highest level since July 29. The yen was also held back by comments from policymakers worried about its recent strength.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2  told Reuters in an interview that the government will respond "appropriately" to unwelcome yen gains that hurt economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Koichi Hamada, an adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , said the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  could consider buying foreign bonds as an option to weaken the yen, if government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is deemed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be exchange rate manipulation. (Editing by Meredith Mazzilli) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-30T20:02:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160830ec8u010t3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
