\par\par \b \uc2 Morning News Call - India, May 24\b0\par\par\uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2016\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par To access the newsletter, click on the link:\par  \par  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_05242016.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://share.thomsonreuters.com/assets/newsletters/Indiamorning/MNC_IN_05242016.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par     \par     FACTORS TO WATCH\par    11:00 am: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Punjab National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  management at post earnings analyst meet in\par Mumbai.\par    4:45 pm: Bank of India media conference after quarterly earnings in Mumbai.\par    GMF: ASIA LIVECHAT - BETTING FOCUS with Patrick Jay, Consultant to global,\par digital and land based betting, gaming and sports sectors\par Patrick is a big name in betting circles having worked as sports and football\par director for Ladbrokes and recently as Director of Trading at the Hong Kong\par Jockey Club. Currently an acting consultant, we speak to Patrick at 1330 IST\par about the future of betting after the inroad of mobiles and tablets, on whether\par the Chinese whip on corruption has affected the business in Macau and whether\par Football has fat tails! (i.e. Leicester winning again!). To join the\par conversation, click on the link: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/communities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://forms.thomsonreuters.com/communities/}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par    INDIA TOP NEWS\par      India puts off \f28 \uc2 \f2 GM\f28 \uc2 \f2  cotton seed order, easing pressure on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Monsanto\par India\f28 \uc2 \f2  has temporarily withdrawn an order capping royalties on any new variety of\par genetically-modified cotton seeds, a government source said on Monday, bringing\par relief to U.S.-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Monsanto Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the market's sole supplier. \par      Taiwan to launch futures contracts for U.S, India benchmark indexes \par Taiwan will launch futures contracts for trading on the island of benchmark\par stock indexes from the U.S. and India, a senior Taiwanese securities official\par said on Monday. \par      India to boost Iran port project, links to Afghanistan \par Indian Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday pledged up to $500 million to\par develop the southern Iran port of Chabahar, in a move to give his country trade\par access to Iran, Afghanistan and central Asia. \par      NALCO to explore building smelter in Iran\par National Aluminium Co Ltd and Iran's mining development body have agreed to\par explore the possibility of building an aluminium smelter in Iran, NALCO said in\par a statement on Monday, as New Delhi tries to boost trade ties with Tehran after\par the lifting of sanctions. \par      India braces for more heat after temperatures break records\par India was bracing on Monday for another bout of extreme heat after temperatures\par smashed records in some parts of the country, while weather officials warned\par against more frequent heat waves. \par     \par    GLOBAL TOP NEWS\par      Obama to lay out vision for Vietnam ties after ending arms ban\par U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barack Obama\f28 \uc2 \f2  is set to lay out more of his plan for a stronger\par alliance with Vietnam on Tuesday, after scrapping an arms ban that was the last\par big hurdle between two countries drawn together by concern over China's military\par buildup. \par      U.S. says late \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taliban\f28 \uc2 \f2  leader was planning attacks on Americans\par U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barack Obama\f28 \uc2 \f2  approved the drone strike that killed Mullah Akhtar\par Mansour because the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taliban\f28 \uc2 \f2  leader was overseeing plans for new attacks on\par American targets in Kabul, the Afghan capital, U.S. officials said on\par Monday. \par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangladesh Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  heist trail goes cold in Manila as probes falter\par More than three months have passed since $81 million was stolen in a brazen\par cyber-heist from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangladesh's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sent to Manila - yet authorities\par in the Philippines appear no closer to nabbing those who laundered most of the\par money through a bank and casinos here. \par     \par    LOCAL MARKETS OUTLOOK\par     (As reported by NewsRise)\par      The SGX Nifty Futures was trading at 7,727.00, down 0.13 pct from its\par previous close.\par      The Indian rupee will likely edge lower against the U.S. dollar, tracking\par its Asian peers, as expectations of an imminent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate increase\par continue to support the greenback. \par      Indian government bonds will likely open higher, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par announced an open market purchase of notes this week ahead of a state debt\par auction where the quantum is lower than scheduled.The yield on the benchmark\par 7.59 pct bond maturing in 2026 is likely to trade in a 7.43 pct-7.47 pct range.\par     \par    GLOBAL MARKETS\par      Wall Street ended lower on Monday as a bounce in Apple failed to offset\par concerns that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could raise interest rates sooner than\par later. \par      Asian shares were nearly flat in early trading, while the dollar rebounded\par from steep losses against the yen in the previous session. \par      The yen held on to gains, shored up by investors' risk aversion and\par receding expectations that Japan will weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a fresh warning\par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par      Short-dated \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields rose on Monday, with the two-year yield\par hovering at its highest in two months, as traders bet the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may\par raise interest rates as early as June if the economy shows further improvement.\par  \par      Oil prices were little changed in thin early Asian trade as a firmer\par dollar weighed on oil markets while a likely drawdown in U.S. crude and gasoline\par stockpiles pointed to stronger demand ahead of the U.S. summer driving season.\par  \par      Gold slipped in early trade to trade near a 3-1/2 week low hit a day\par earlier, as prices remained under pressure on expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will increase interest rates as early as June. \par         \par                    CLOSE        FII INVESTMENTS  EQUITIES     DEBT\par  PNDF spot         67.44/67.47  May 23           -$9.71 mln   -$22.08 mln\par  10-yr bond yield  7.65 pct     Month-to-date    $167.89 mln  -$742.5 mln\par                                 Year-to-date     $1.97 bln    -$1.09 bln\par     \par     \par     For additional data:\par     India govt bond market volumes       \par     Stock market reports                 \par     Non-deliverable forwards data        \par     Corporate debt stories               [IN CORPD]\par     Local market closing/intraday levels [IN SNAPSHOT]\par     Monthly inflows                      [INFLOWS RTRS TABLE IN]\par \par ($1 = 67.49 Indian rupees)\par \par  (Reporting by Nishit Kunal in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-24T04:21:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160524ec5o008kf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
