\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-PREVIEW-Japan to struggle to overcome G7 rift on yen, fiscal policy\b0\par\par\uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2016\par 03:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * G7 finance leaders to meet May 20-21\par \par \uc2 * Japan, U.S. seen failing to bridge gap on yen\par \par \uc2 * No G7 consensus on size of fiscal spending\par \par \uc2 * G7 seen settling on vague agreement for reforms\par \par \uc2 * Finmin Aso, BOJ Kuroda to meet press May 21\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 17 (Reuters) - A weekend gathering of G7 finance leaders may expose a rift on issues ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fiscal policies within the close-knit group of advanced economies, dashing Japan's hopes of mustering a coordinated policy response to spur global growth.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew, Federal Reserve Chairman Janet Yellen and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  will be among \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  finance leaders gathering in Sendai, northern Japan on May 20-21.\par \par \uc2 Japan has failed to bridge differences with the United States on the yen, with Washington dismissing Tokyo's concerns that recent yen rises are excessive and instead pushing for agreements against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rift may be evident at the weekend G7 meeting, diminishing prospects of an agreement beyond reiterating the importance for exchange-rate stability.\par \par \uc2 There is also no consensus on how much fiscal stimulus the global economy needs with Germany resisting calls from Japan and the United States for bigger spending.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers are taming market expectations, saying Tokyo never intended the G7 nations to agree on joint fiscal action it sees as only possible in times of crises such as the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The G7 will likely settle with a vague agreement on the need to deploy a "balanced" dose of monetary, fiscal and structural policies, officials involved in the negotiations say.\par \par \uc2 The result could be another meeting in which officials claim progress in pushing an agenda of structural reforms, rather than concrete steps to avoid a global recession.\par \par \uc2 "It's just a way to say you did something when you did very little," said Tamim Bayoumi, a visiting fellow at the Peterson Institute, a Washington think tank for international economics.\par \par \uc2 While no communique will be released, Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  hopes to lay the grounds for a G7 leaders' summit to be held next week, where measures to address stagnant global growth will be high on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 For Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mandarins, the top priority in Sendai is to garner a G7 agreement on the importance of "exchange-rate stability," officials with knowledge of the negotiations say.\par \par \uc2 That will give Tokyo justification to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it considers any yen gains as excessive.\par \par \uc2 It may also be the most the G7 nations can agree on given differences between Tokyo and Washington on what is defined as excessively volatile yen moves.\par \par \uc2 Lew said on Friday his views have not changed on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies since a G20 meeting in April, when he told Aso that markets were "orderly" despite a rising yen.\par \par \uc2 He also said Japan has relied too heavily on monetary policy and needed to focus more on boosting domestic demand and pursuing structural reforms.\par \par \uc2 Japan insists that recent yen gains have been speculative and that a \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  report including it in a new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch list did not constrain its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Aso has repeatedly threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen rises.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably keep emphasising that countries shouldn't resort to competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations, while Japan will argue that excess volatility is undesirable," said a G7 source familiar with the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 "But no country, including the United States, will disagree strongly that exchange-rate stability is important," he said.\par \par \uc2 Japan had hoped to garner a G7 agreement on the need to ramp up fiscal spending but has received a cool response from Germany, which insists on fiscal discipline.\par \par \uc2 If the G7 nations share their concerns over weak global growth, however, premier \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  may use it to justify delaying a sales tax hike and deploy fiscal stimulus to resuscitate Japan's fragile recovery, some analysts say. (Additional reporting by Izumi Nakagawa and Takashi Umekawa in Tokyo, David Lawder and Jason Lange in Washington; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-20T01:35:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160517ec5h004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
