\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-U.S. says further yuan appreciation 'key' to rebalancing China's economy\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2015\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds China Foreign Ministry comment)\par \par \uc2 By Lindsay Dunsmuir\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The United States called on China on Monday to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate further as a crucial support to the world's second-biggest economy in rebalancing its economy.\par \par \uc2 In the Treasury's semi-annual report on economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of major trade partners, the United States also said that the yuan, officially known as the renminbi, remains below its "appropriate medium-term valuation."\par \par \uc2 The language is a shift from the previous report in April, when the United States said the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was significantly undervalued.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury, in its regular scorecard, did not label any major trading partner a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator but called on countries with current account surpluses, which include Germany and South Korea, to do more to boost flagging global growth.\par \par \uc2 The roughly $50 per barrel decline in the price of oil is shifting income of over $600 billion annually from oil exporters to oil importers, the Treasury said.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury estimated that non-FDI capital outflows from China likely hit $520-530 billion in first eight months of this year, including $200 billion in August alone.\par \par \uc2 "Market factors are exerting downward pressure on the RMB at present, but these are likely to be transitory," it said.\par \par \uc2 Worries over China's economic slowdown and possible interest rate rises by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  have led to a wave of capital outflows that intensified after Beijing's surprise devaluation of the yuan on Aug. 11.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  afterwards, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks sold a record net 761.3 billion yuan ($119.85 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, data showed on Friday, as capital outflows weighed on the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  forcefully both in the domestic and global yuan markets.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew has been urging China to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, to float more freely.\par \par \uc2 Many U.S. lawmakers have repeatedly complained that China deliberately undervalues its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain a competitive advantage in international markets. The last time the Treasury labeled a country a manipulator was China in 1994.\par \par \uc2 "We will continue to steadily advance yuan exchange rate mechanism reform according to relevant principles," Chinese Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Hua Chunying told a regular news briefing on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Before the devaluation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been slowly appreciating as the Chinese government sought to support its aim of shifting the economy's main engine from exports to domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 "Further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation is key...and will support the purchasing power of Chinese consumers and help shift production towards non-traded goods and services," the report said.\par \par \uc2 China is pushing for the yuan to be included in the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's benchmark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket as a means of reducing its dependence on the dollar, but policymakers have yet to decide if it has met all the market-based criteria.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the report, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  again called for South Korea to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and repeated that the won appeared to be "undervalued" and should be allowed to appreciate over the medium term.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  also urged Japan to recalibrate fiscal policy to support economic growth and reduce reliance on yen depreciation to boost exports. (Reporting by Lindsay Dunsmuir, Krista Hughes and Kevin Yao and Michael Martina in BEIJING; Editing by Diane Craft & Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-20T11:37:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151019ebaj00pkc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
