     profit increased by GBP55 million and the adjusted return on equity was \par      15.3%, driven by improved income, lower expenses and lower impairments. \par  \par --  Total income was GBP14 million, or 3%, higher. Net interest income increased \par      by GBP27 million due to a combination of improved deposit margins following \par      a re-pricing exercise in the UK and lower treasury charges. Non-interest \par      income declined by GBP13 million reflecting the impact of adverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par      exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements and lower transactional activity in the international \par      business. \par  \par --  Total expenses declined by 8% to GBP400 million. Adjusted expenses were \par      down GBP34 million, 8%, at GBP397 million reflecting savings from the streamlining \par      of the property footprint, favourable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements, reduced \par      headcount and the continued management of discretionary costs. \par  \par --  Impairment charges declined by GBP7 million as a result of fewer specific \par      impairments. \par  \par --  Client assets and liabilities were 7% lower than the previous year, with \par      the decrease in assets under management driven by low margin custody asset \par      outflows, adverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements, portfolio exits and reduced \par      balances in the UK. Deposits were GBP3.0 billion lower, largely as a result \par      of re-pricing action in the UK. Lending declined by GBP0.5 billion as repayments \par      outstripped new lending in the latter part of 2013. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Q2 2014 compared with Q1 2014\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par --  Operating profit was GBP70 million for the quarter, GBP5 million lower, \par      largely as a result of a small increase in impairments and expenses, with \par      income broadly flat. \par  \par --  Total expenses were up GBP2 million, wholly as a result of increased restructuring \par      costs. \par  \par --  Client assets and liabilities were 1% lower than the prior quarter, wholly \par      driven by a GBP0.7 billion reduction in deposits following the UK re-pricing \par      exercise and outflows in the international business. Assets under management \par      increased by GBP0.2 billion due to positive market movements. Lending remained \par      broadly flat. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Q2 2014 compared with Q2 2013\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par --  Operating profit increased by GBP23 million benefitting from higher income, \par      lower costs and lower impairments. \par  \par --  Total income was GBP3 million, 1%, higher. Net interest income rose by GBP15 \par      million due to improved deposit margins following a re-pricing exercise \par      in the UK and lower treasury charges. Non-interest income declined by GBP12 \par      million largely as a result of adverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements and lower \par      transactional activity in the international business. \par  \par --  Total expenses declined by GBP19 million reflecting savings from the streamlining \par      of the property footprint, reduced headcount, beneficial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par      movements and the continued tight management of discretionary costs. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corporate & Institutional Banking\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   Half year ended         Quarter ended \par                                  =================  ========================== \par                                   30 June  30 June  30 June  31 March  30 June \par                                      2014     2013     2014      2014     2013 \par                                      GBPm     GBPm     GBPm      GBPm 