f. \par  \par --  RWA equivalent decreased by GBP21 billion, or 33%, to GBP44 billion during \par      H1 2014. This primarily reflects disposals and run-off, supplemented by \par      methodology changes and lower \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and market risk RWAs. \par  \par --  The operating loss of GBP48 million benefited from GBP281 million of disposal \par      gains and recoveries in H1 2014 with underlying impairments of GBP301 million. \par  \par --  The net effect of the operating loss and RWA equivalent (RWAe) reduction \par      resulted in net CET1 accretion of GBP2 billion. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Q2 2014 compared with Q1 2014\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Capital \par --  RWAe reduction of GBP7 billion, to GBP44 billion, reflects a combination \par      of disposals, run-off and lower market risk RWAs. \par  \par --  The operating focus in the quarter was on capital intensive positions to \par      maximise the capital accretion benefit. Reductions in these positions were \par      achieved in a capital accretive manner and consistent with our asset management \par      principles. Disposal activity was spread across all sectors, with the most \par      notable reductions in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ulster Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Real Estate business pillars. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Funded assets\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par --  Funded assets fell to GBP21 billion, a reduction of GBP3 billion, or 14%, \par      during the quarter. \par  \par --  The reduction was achieved by a mixture of run-off and disposals, and continued \par      to benefit from a combination of strong liquidity in the market and asset \par      demand in specific sectors. The first major disposal in Ireland was completed \par      in Q2 2014 which reduced funded assets by GBP0.5 billion. \par  \par --  The percentage mix of assets across each of the business pillars remained \par      broadly stable. \par  \par  \par Operating performance \par --  Operating profit for the second quarter was GBP66 million, a GBP180 million \par      improvement compared with Q1 2014 and included a GBP36 million latent provision \par      release reflecting improving credit conditions. The operating performance \par      also benefited from a number of disposal gains and recoveries with good \par      pricing in the market and efficient execution. \par  \par --  The favourable market conditions were reflected in higher than anticipated \par      sale prices for assets disposed of in the quarter, resulting in disposal \par      gains of GBP225 million, primarily through the write back of impairment \par      provisions, compared with GBP56 million in Q1 2014. \par  \par --  The net effect of the operating profit of GBP66 million and RWAe reduction \par      of GBP7 billion(1) resulted in net CET1 accretion of GBP0.8 billion in the \par      quarter. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Funding employed\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par --  RCR continues to be funded primarily by RBS Treasury \par      and has no material third party deposits. \par  \par --  A run off profile of 85% over three years has \par     been assumed for RCR's asset base with the associated \par     funding cost being calculated from Treasury issuance \par     maturing in line with the run down of the RCR \par     balance sheet. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par (1)  Capital equivalent - GBP0.7 billion at an internal CET1 ratio of 10%. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IR BFLBBZVFBBBF [ 01-08-14 0601GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020140801ea810004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
