\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Turkish lira weakens beyond 2 per dollar on Washington's Syria comments\b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Lira at record low\par \par \uc2 * Syria weighs\par \par \uc2 * C.bank governor to speak\par \par \uc2 By Seda Sezer\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Aug 27 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira weakened beyond 2 to the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled possible military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria and the market waited for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry, in the most forceful reaction yet to last week's suspected gas attack outside Damascus, said President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  "believes there must be accountability for those who would use the world's most heinous weapons against the world's most vulnerable people".\par \par \uc2 The lira was at 2.0045 against the dollar by 0544 GMT after dropping as low as 2.0095 earlier and from 1.9918 late on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Erdem Basci was expected to appear on television at 0730 GMT, and investors are looking for more guidance on how he will act to stop the lira's decline.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been tightening monetary conditions to support the lira through a range of tools, but has left its main benchmark rate - the one-week repo rate - unchanged at 4.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The recent developments in Syria signal possible military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and this is negative for economies like Turkey," said Fatih Keresteci, a strategist at \uc2 HSBC Bank\uc2  in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hyperactive monetary policy, which aims to reduce the selling pressure, creates a second wave of selling tendency because it creates uncertainties. The lira will remain under pressure unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  switches to an orthodox policy and makes lira relatively attractive again."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction on Monday and sold $350 million, in line with additional monetary tightening steps announced last week. The bank also held its first one-week, fixed-rate repo auction in almost a week, with a volume of 1.5 billion lira ($755 million).\par \par \uc2 It also said it would launch a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling auction on Tuesday with a minimum volume of $50 million.\par \par \uc2 Growing expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve may soon start tapering its stimulus programme has hit appetite for emerging markets, with Turkey's gaping current account deficit leaving it particularly vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 The country is dependent on foreign inflows to finance the gap, which is equivalent to around 7.1 percent of Turkey's economic output.\par \par \uc2 Raising interest rates makes lira assets more attractive to foreign investors, but could also crimp growth, something Prime Minister Tayyip Erdogan's government is eager to avoid before local polls next year and a general election in 2015.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-TURKEY/LIRA (UPDATE 1) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130827e98r0006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
