\par\par \b \uc2 Spot Gold Hits Near Three-month High on US Data, Syria Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francesca Freeman   \par \uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 11:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The price of gold hit its highest level in almost three months on the European spot market Tuesday as investors sought a safe store of value amid signs of economic weakness in the U.S. and escalating tensions in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold rose 0.6% to $1,412.70 a troy ounce in early trade, its highest price since June 7. At 0857 GMT, the yellow metal was up 0.4% at $1,410.80 an ounce.\par \par \uc2 Gold prices rose as European investors--some of whom were just returning to their desks after a long weekend in the U.K.--reacted to Monday's poor set of U.S. new-homes sales and durable goods orders data, as well as signs that U.S. is considering military action against Syria.\par \par \uc2 While the U.S. data sparked hopes for a prolonged period of gold-supportive economic stimulus by the Federal Reserve, concerns over conflict in the Middle East raised demand for traditional insecurity hedges, such as gold, said market participants.\par \par \uc2 "The possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its allies in the Syria conflict only adds further weight to the upside [for gold prices]," said \uc2 Gary Dugan\uc2 , chief investment officer for Asia and Middle East at U.K.-based wealth management firm \uc2 Coutts & Co\uc2 . "There are very few ways of hedging downside risk in portfolios from such geopolitical tension other than to buy gold."\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the U.S. stepped up its rhetoric on Syria with Secretary of State John Kerry saying the Syrian government's use of chemical weapons against civilians was a "moral obscenity" and there was conclusive evidence that chemical weapons were used last week to kill hundreds of civilians.\par \par \uc2 Gold prices also derived support from news of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of gold in July.\par \par \uc2 The central banks of Russia, Azerbaijan and Kazakhstan returned to the gold market once again last month, topping up their stockpiles of the precious metal as prices traded near three-year lows.\par \par \uc2 Russia, one of the world's largest owners of gold bullion, increased its holdings by the most since April, adding more than 200,000 troy ounces of the metal to its official reserves, which now stand at 32.2 million ounces, according to data from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Central banks, largely in developing economies, have increased their gold holdings over the past few years as debt crises have helped put pressure on reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the U.S. dollar and the euro.\par \par \uc2 In other precious metals Tuesday, spot silver was down 0.1% at $24.275 an ounce at 0847 GMT, spot platinum was 0.2% higher at $1,546.50 an ounce and spot palladium was down 0.04% at $745.19 an ounce.\par \par \uc2 --Rhiannon Hoyle contributed to this report.\par \par \uc2 Write to Francesca Freeman at francesca.freeman@wsj.com [ 08-27-13 0511ET ]\par \par \uc2 1090 61045 82270   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020130827e98r00029\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
