 used for 2013 is 25% (2012: 25%).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During the period,the Group recognised a current tax charge of US$70.2 million (1H 2012: US$87.5 million) and a deferred tax charge of US$18.2 million (1H 2012: US$17.9 million). [ 06-08-13 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During 2008, the effective tax rate applicable to the Group's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Turkmenistan was increased by 5% to 25% by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hydrocarbon Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  Law of 2008. The Group has continued to apply this rate in determining its tax liabilities as at 30 June 2013. The Group is in discussions with the authorities in Turkmenistan about the applicability of this rate to periods prior to 2008, but it does not believe that prior periods are affected by this increase. A provision of US$11.1 million has been made in respect of the additional tax that could become payable if the increased tax rate were applied to prior periods.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    17         Related party transactions \par    a)         Transactions and balances \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company's largest shareholder is \f28 \uc2 \f2 Emirates National Oil Company Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ENOC) L.L.C ("ENOC"), which owns approximately 53.99% of the Company's ordinary share capital. ENOC is ultimately a wholly owned entity of the Government of Dubai. Two members of the Board, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mr. Ahmad Sharaf\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mr. Mohammed Al Ghurair\f28 \uc2 \f2  are nominees of ENOC. All transactions with related parties are on an arm's length basis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  (i) The following transactions are with ENOC and its subsidiaries: \par  \par                                                                                Unaudited           Unaudited \par                                                                                 6 months            6 months \par                                                    