nt that they affect the fair value of the Company's fixed rate borrowings, may also affect the amount by which the Company's share price is at a discount or a premium to the net asset value (assuming that the Company's share price is unaffected by movements in interest rates).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The interest rate risk profile of the Company's financial assets and liabilities at 30 April is shown below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Financial assets                            2013                                 2012 \par                                                         Weighted                             Weighted \par                                             Weighted     average                 Weighted     average \par                                    Fair      average      period        Fair      average      period \par                                   value     interest       until       value     interest       until \par                                 GBP'000         rate    maturity     GBP'000         rate    maturity \par ---------------------------  ----------  -----------  ----------  ----------  -----------  ---------- \par  Fixed rate: \par  UK bonds                             -            -           -       1,194         8.5%    15 years \par  European bonds                   1,075        54.2%     2 years      10,641        12.6%     5 years \par  US bonds                        10,088         9.9%    14 years      11,407         0.4%     3 years \par  UK swap rate linked \par   note(*)                         4,600         7.2%     4 years       4,291         7.2%     5 years \par ---------------------------  ----------  -----------  ----------  ----------  -----------  ---------- \par  Floating rate: \par  European bonds (interest \par   rate linked to Euro \par   LIBOR)                          5,670        26.4%     3 years       5,272        21.4%     3 years \par  Brazilian bonds (interest \par   rate linked to Brazilia