ments made under these operating leases are recognised in profit or loss on a straight line basis over the term of the lease. Benefits received as an incentive to sign a lease, whatever form they may take, are credited to profit or loss on a straight line basis over the lease term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On 25 January 2006, the Group signed a lease on new premises at Morgan House, Madeira Walk, Windsor, Berkshire. This lease expires on 19 June 2016. The annual commitment under this lease is GBP229,710 (2012: GBP229,710).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group has considered the risks and rewards of ownership of the leased property, and considers that they remain with the lessor, consequently, this lease is recognised as an operating lease.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 31 March 2013 the Group had commitments under non-cancellable operating leases relating to land and buildings as set out below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                          2013      2012 \par                                       GBP'000   GBP'000 \par -----------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Not later than one year                  230       230 \par  Later than one year and not later \par   than five years                         517       747 \par                                           747       977 \par -----------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 26. Related parties transactions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Company\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Details of transactions between the Company and other Group undertakings, which are related parties of the Company, are shown below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transactions with subsidiaries\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company's subsidiary undertakings are listed in note 13, which includes a description of the nature of their business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                 2013      2012 \par                                              GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ------------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Amounts due from subsidiaries                 1,661     1,188 \par  Amounts due to subsidiaries                 (1,717)     (948) \par  Interest received from subsidiaries \par   on intercompany loan balances                    9         5 \par  Net dividends received from subsidiaries      1,465     8,610 \par ------------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amounts owed to and by related parties will be settled in cash. No guarantees have been given or received. No provisions for doubtful debts have been raised against amounts outstanding (2012: nil), and no expense has been recognised during the period in respect of bad or doubtful debts due from related parties (2012: nil).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transactions with seeded funds\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From time to time, the Group injects capital into funds operated by the Group to trial new products (seed capital). If the Group is able to exercise control over such a seeded fund by holding a majority interest (whether the majority interest is held by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  alone, or by combining the interests of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its Directors), then the fund is considered to be a related party.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - FTSE FRB10 Index Fund and Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - Emerging Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund are both related parties on this basis, but there were no transactions between the Company and these funds during the year. Similarly, the Record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund - Euro Stress was a related party until its liquidation in September 2012. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  received GBP854,213 on liquidation of its holding in the fund.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Group\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transactions or balances between Group entities have been eliminated on consolidation and in accordance with IAS 24, are not disclosed in this note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The compensation given to key management personnel is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                     2013      2012 \par                                  GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Short-term employee benefits      3,435     4,007 \par  Post-employment benefits            289       342 \par  Share-based payments                901     1,057 \par  Dividends                           873     3,792 \par ------------------------------  --------  -------- \par                                    5,498     9,198 \par ------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Directors' remuneration\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                              2013      2012 \par                                           GBP'000   GBP'000 \par ---------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  Aggregate emoluments of the Directors \par  Emoluments (excluding pension \par   contribution)                             2,423     2,618 \par  Gains made on exercise of share \par   options                                       9        18 \par  Pension contribution                         121       146 \par ---------------------------------------  --------  -------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During the year, five Directors of the Company (2012: four) participated in the Group Personal Pension Plan, a defined contribution scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27. Capital management\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's objectives when managing capital are (i) to safeguard the Group's ability to continue as a going concern, (ii) to provide an adequate return to its shareholders, and (iii) to meet regulatory capital requirements set by the UK Financial Conduct Authority (previously the Financial Services Authority).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group sets the amount of capital in proportion to risk. The Group manages the capital structure and makes adjustments to it in light of changes in economic conditions and the risk characteristics of the underlying assets. In order to maintain or adjust the capital structure, the Group may adjust the amount of dividends paid to shareholders, return capital to shareholders, or issue new shares. The Group had no debt in the current or prior financial year and consequently does not calculate a debt-to-adjusted capital ratio.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For regulatory capital purposes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Record plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  is subject to consolidated financial supervision by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Conduct Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ). Our regulatory capital requirements are in accordance with \f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2  rules consistent with the Capital Requirements Directive. Our financial resources have exceeded our financial resource requirements (regulatory capital requirements) at all times during the year. Further information is provided in the Business Review.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 28. Ultimate controlling party\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at 31 March 2013 the Company had no ultimate controlling party, nor at 31 March 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 29. Post reporting date events\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No adjusting or significant non-adjusting events have occurred between the reporting date and the date of authorisation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 30. Statutory Accounts\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This statement was approved by the Board on 10 June 2013. The financial information set out above does not constitute the Company's statutory accounts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The statutory accounts for the financial year ended 31 March 2012 have been delivered to the Registrar of Companies, and those for the year ended in 31 March 2013 will be delivered in due course. The auditor has reported on those accounts; the reports were unqualified, did not include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report, and did not contain statements under section 498(2) or 498(3) of the Companies Act 2006 in respect of either set of accounts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Notes to Editors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This announcement includes information with respect to Record's financial condition, its results of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and business, strategy, plans and objectives. All statements in this document, other than statements of historical fact, including words such as "anticipates", "expects", "intends", "plans", "believes", "seeks", "estimates", "may", "will", "continue", "project" and similar expressions, are forward-looking statements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These forward-looking statements are not guarantees of the Company's future performance and are subject to risks, uncertainties and assumptions that could cause the actual future results, performance or achievements of the Company to differ materially from those expressed in or implied by such forward-looking statements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The forward-looking statements contained in this document are based on numerous assumptions regarding Record's present and future business and strategy and speak only as at the date of this announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company expressly disclaims any obligation or undertaking to disseminate any updates or revisions to any forward-looking statements contained in this announcement whether as a result of new information, future events or otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FR SFWFWSFDSEFM [ 11-06-13 0600GMT ]\f28 \par