he portion payable in the form of shares, will be deferred in time, with the deferred portion being paid in equal amounts over a three-year period. Hence, the non-deferred portion of the 2011 bonus will be paid in 2012, while the deferred portion will be paid in three instalments in 2013, 2014 and 2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The costs met by the Bank during 2011 corresponding to the coverage of pension commitments in respect of the beneficiary Directors Ron and Aparicio amount to EUR251,000. These same directors are also the beneficiaries of life and health insurance premiums totalling EUR8,000.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The vested rights and mathematical reserves linked to the pension rights of current Directors Messrs. Ron, Aparicio and Higuera amount to EUR5,659, EUR1,946 and EUR10,134 thousand, respectively, making up a total of EUR17.7 million. This figure, added to the EUR37.9 million corresponding to other past directors, makes up a total of EUR55.6 million at 31 December 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Employees\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of employees of the Enlarged Group at 31 March 2012 was 18,059, compared to 14,062 in 31 March 2011. In Spain, the number of employees was 16,236, divided in 10,456 men and 5,780 women. Abroad, the number of employees at 31 March 2012 was 1,823, divided in 1,123 men and 700 women.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Major Shareholders\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Issuer is not aware of the existence of any individual or body corporate exercising, or who could exercise, directly or indirectly, control over it, nor is the Issuer aware of the existence of any agreement which could lead to a change of control at a subsequent date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial Information Concerning the Issuer's Assets and Liabilities, Financial Position and Profits and Losses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The audited consolidated annual accounts of the Issuer and of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Pastor\f28 \uc2 \f2  for the financial years ended 31 December 2011 (which 