\par\par \b \uc2 UMECO PLC\uc2  Recommended Cash Offer for \uc2 Umeco plc\uc2  Recommended Cash Offer for\b0\par\par\uc2 20,909 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2012\par 08:01\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012   \par \par \uc2 TIDMUMC TIDMTTM\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 1912B\par \par \uc2 UMECO PLC\par \par \uc2 12 April 2012\par \par \uc2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OF SUCH JURISDICTION\par \par \uc2 12 April 2012\par \par \uc2 RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER\par \par \uc2 FOR\par \par \uc2 UMECO PLC\par \par \uc2 BY\par \par \uc2 CYTEC UK HOLDINGS LIMITED\par \par \uc2 a wholly-owned subsidiary of\par \par \uc2 CYTEC INDUSTRIES INC\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 (to be effected by way of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006)\par \par \uc2 The boards of \uc2 Umeco plc\uc2  ("\uc2 Umeco\uc2 ") and \uc2 Cytec Industries Inc\uc2  . ("\uc2 Cytec\uc2  ") are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash offer by \uc2 Cytec UK Holdings Limited\uc2  ("\uc2 Cytec\uc2  Bidco"), a wholly--owned subsidiary of \uc2 Cytec\uc2  , for the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \uc2 Umeco\uc2 . It is intended that the Acquisition will be effected by way of a Court-sanctioned scheme of arrangement of \uc2 Umeco\uc2  under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006.\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 -- Under the terms of the Acquisition, Umeco Shareholders will be entitled to receive 550 pence in cash for each Umeco Share held at the Reduction Record Time, valuing the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \uc2 Umeco\uc2  at approximately GBP274 million.\par \par \uc2 -- The consideration of 550 pence in cash for each Umeco Share represents a premium of approximately:\par \par \uc2 - 46.3 per cent. to the Closing Price of 376 pence per Umeco Share on 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement;\par \par \uc2 - 52.2 per cent. to the average Closing Price of approximately 361 pence per Umeco Share for the three month period to 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement; and\par \par \uc2 - 61.3 per cent. to the average Closing Price of approximately 341 pence per Umeco Share for the six month period to 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement.\par \par \uc2 -- There will be no final dividend payable on the Umeco Shares if the Acquisition is completed. If a dividend on Umeco Shares is declared or is otherwise payable before the Acquisition is completed the Offer Price shall be reduced by the amount of that dividend.\par \par \uc2 -- The Board of Umeco, which has been so advised by Rothschild and Investec, considers the terms of the Acquisition to be fair and reasonable. In providing financial advice to the Board of Umeco, Rothschild and Investec have taken into account the commercial assessments of the Board of Umeco. Rothschild and Investec are providing the independent financial advice for the purposes of Rule 3 of the Code and Investec is also acting as sole broker to Umeco. Accordingly, the Board of Umeco intends unanimously to recommend that Umeco Shareholders vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Special Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting, as those members of the Board of Umeco who hold Umeco Shares have undertaken so to do in respect of their own beneficial holdings of 137,314 Umeco Shares (representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.3 per cent. of the Umeco Shares currently in issue).\par \par \uc2 -- In addition, \uc2 Cytec\uc2  has also received irrevocable undertakings to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Special Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting from \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , Hermes and Aberforth in respect of a total of 14,518,196 Umeco Shares (as at or around the date of this Announcement) representing, in aggregate, approximately 29.9 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \uc2 Umeco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -- As at the date of this Announcement \uc2 Cytec\uc2  has therefore received, in aggregate, irrevocable undertakings to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Special Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting in respect of a total of 14,655,510 Umeco Shares (as at or around the date of this Announcement) representing, in aggregate, approximately 30.2per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \uc2 Umeco\uc2 . Further details of these irrevocable undertakings are set out in Appendix III to this Announcement.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --      The Acquisition will be funded using \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2   Bidco's existing cash resources. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- It is intended that the Acquisition will be effected by way of a scheme of arrangement of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006. The Scheme will require the approval of Scheme Shareholders and the sanction of the Court. Upon the Scheme becoming effective, it will be binding on all Scheme Shareholders, irrespective of whether they attend or vote at the Court Meeting or the General Meeting (and if they attended and voted, whether or not they voted in favour).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  is an international provider of advanced composite materials primarily to the aerospace and defence, wind energy, automotive, recreation and other industrial sectors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a global speciality chemicals and materials company focused on developing, manufacturing and selling value-added products. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's products serve a diverse range of end markets including aerospace composites, structural adhesives, automotive and industrial coatings, electronics, inks, mining and plastics. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  operates on a global basis with manufacturing and research facilities located in 14 countries. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is listed on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  and, as at the Business Day before this Announcement, has a market capitalisation of approximately US$2.6 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco is a private limited company incorporated in England and Wales which is wholly-owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco is itself a holding company that owns \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's UK operating company as well as interests in several other \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  European operating entities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Board of Cytec believes that the combined \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be able to offer customers superior solutions and will be well positioned to capture the substantial growth opportunities in composite materials markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- It is currently anticipated that the Scheme Document (including notices of the Shareholder Meetings) will be posted to Umeco Shareholders and, for information only to participants in the Umeco Share Schemes, as soon as is reasonably practicable and in any event within 28 days of this Announcement and that the Scheme will become effective in the third quarter of 2012, subject to the satisfaction (or, if applicable, waiver) of the Conditions set out in Appendix I to this Announcement. The latest date for the Scheme to become effective and the Acquisition to be completed will be 12 October 2012, or such later date (if any) as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  may, with the consent of the Panel, agree and (if required) the Court may allow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Neil Johnson\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Non-Executive Chairman of Umeco, said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Board of Umeco believes that the offer from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  of 550 pence per Umeco Share is an attractive price for Umeco Shareholders, and represents a valuation that reflects the future growth potential of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  whilst providing certainty, in cash, to Umeco Shareholders."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on the Acquisition, Shane Fleming, Chairman, President and Chief Executive Officer of Cytec, said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are excited about combining \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's existing advanced composites businesses. It greatly improves our presence in the industrial sector, where we see tremendous potential for significant value creation in applications like automotive as customers seek to reduce weight and CO2 emissions. In addition, the Acquisition also enhances our near-term composite capacity while we complete capital investments over the next few years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This transaction is consistent with our strategy to focus on profitable and growing segments where we can leverage our technological leadership. The acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will provide us with additional scale, a dedicated supply chain well-tailored to the needs of the high performance industrial sector and application development capabilities that will help us respond quickly and effectively to customers' needs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This transaction is an important step forward as we position \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  with an industry-leading portfolio of growth businesses by focusing on our engineered materials, in process separation and additive technology segments. We will continue to build on our recent success in capturing new business and penetrating the market with our advanced technology solutions as we seek to deliver enhanced value to our stakeholders."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  is acting as sole financial adviser and corporate broker to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rothschild is acting as joint financial adviser to Umeco. Investec is acting as joint financial adviser and sole corporate broker to Umeco.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This summary should be read in conjunction with, and is subject to, the full text of this Announcement. In particular, the Acquisition is subject to Conditions and further terms set out in Appendix I to this Announcement and the terms and conditions to be set out in the Scheme Document and Forms of Proxy. The sources of information and bases of calculation in respect of certain financial information contained in this Announcement are set out in Appendix II to this Announcement. A summary of the irrevocable undertakings given by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors and the irrevocable undertakings given by certain other Umeco Shareholders is contained in Appendix III to this Announcement. Certain capitalised terms used in this Announcement are defined in Appendix IV.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There will be a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  investors and analysts conference call which will start promptly at 8:30 a.m. ET / 1:30 p.m. BST today.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interested parties may listen to the conference call by dialling the following numbers:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    US (toll free):     +1 888 894 3692 \par    International:      +1 706 902 4297 \par    Access Code:    70797108 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A live webcast of the conference call may be accessed through the Investor Relations section on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cytec.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cytec.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A presentation will be made available shortly before the conference call via the Investor Relations section on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's website.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The replay will be available for three weeks, two hours after the conclusion of the call at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cytec.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cytec.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Enquiries: [ 12-04-12 0601GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco +1 973 357 3283\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jodi Allen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Investor Relations\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  (sole financial adviser and corporate broker to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  (sole financial adviser and corporate broker to\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco) +44 (0) 20 7623 2323\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark Warham\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 David Whiteley\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jon Bathard-Smith (Corporate Broking)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Umeco +44 (0) 1926 331800\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Andrew Moss\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Steve Bowers\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rothschild (joint financial adviser to Umeco) +44 (0) 20 7280 5000\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Paul Simpson\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stuart Vincent\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alistair Allen\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Investec (joint financial adviser and sole corporate broker to Umeco)          +44 (0) 20 7597 5000 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chris Treneman\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 James Rudd\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hudson Sandler\f28 \uc2 \f2  (public relations adviser to Umeco) +44 (0) 20 7796 4133\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Andrew Hayes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Andrew Leach\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IMPORTANT NOTICE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  , which is authorised and regulated in the United Kingdom by the Financial Services Authority, is acting exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco and no one else in connection with the Acquisi