f2  's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's websites at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cytec.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cytec.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.umeco.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.umeco.com}}}\uc2 \f2 , respectively, by no later than 12:00 p.m. on the Business Day following this Announcement. Neither the contents of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's website, of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website nor of any other website accessible from hyperlinks on either \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website, is incorporated into or forms part of this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 You may request a hard copy of this Announcement (and any information incorporated by reference in this Announcement) by contacting Carlton Nelson at Investec during business hours on +44 (0) 20 7597 5000 or by submitting a request in writing to Carlton Nelson at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Investec Bank plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  , 2 Gresham Street, London EC2V 7QP. It is important that you note that unless you make such a request, a hard copy of this Announcement and any such information incorporated by reference in it will not be sent to you. You may also request that all future documents, announcements and information to be sent to you in relation to the Acquisition should be in hard copy form.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY IN, INTO OR FROM ANY JURISDICTION WHERE TO DO SO WOULD CONSTITUTE A VIOLATION OF THE RELEVANT LAWS OF SUCH JURISDICTION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12 April 2012\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RECOMMENDED CASH OFFER\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FOR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UMECO PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CYTEC UK HOLDINGS LIMITED\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a wholly-owned subsidiary of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CYTEC INDUSTRIES INC\f28 \uc2 \f2  .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (to be effected by way of a scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    1.         Introduction \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Boards of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  are pleased to announce that they have reached agreement on the terms of a recommended cash offer by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco, a wholly owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  , for the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that the Acquisition will be effected by way of a Court-sanctioned scheme of arrangement of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006. The terms of the Acquisition value each Umeco Share at 550 pence andthe entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately GBP274 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         Summary of the terms of the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Scheme will be subject to the satisfaction (or, if applicable, waiver) of the Conditions set out in Appendix I to this Announcement and the full terms and conditions that will be set out in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Scheme becomes effective in accordance with its terms, the Umeco Shares will be cancelled and Umeco Shareholders holding Umeco Shares at the Reduction Record Time will be entitled to receive:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par        for each Umeco Share         550 pence in cash \par  The consideration of 550 pence in cash for each Umeco Share \par   represents a premium of approximately: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 46.3 per cent. to the Closing Price of 376 pence per Umeco Share on 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 52.2 per cent. to the average Closing Price of approximately 361 pence per Umeco Share for the three month period to 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 61.3 per cent. to the average Closing Price of approximately 341 pence per Umeco Share for the six month period to 11 April 2012, being the last Dealing Day prior to this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There will be no final dividend payable on Umeco Shares if the Acquisition is completed. If a dividend on Umeco Shares is declared or is otherwise payable before the Acquisition is completed the Offer Price shall be reduced by the amount of that dividend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         Background to, and reasons for, the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Board of Cytec believes the addition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's business will allow \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  to further enhance and leverage its position as a technology leader in advanced composite materials. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's business will expand \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's presence in the aerospace sector and provide a significant position in non-aerospace sectors, both of which will provide significant growth opportunities in advanced materials. [ 12-04-12 0601GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition is consistent with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's strategy to focus on profitable and growing segments where it can leverage its technological leadership. The Board of Cytec believes the acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  with additional scale, a dedicated supply chain well-tailored to the needs of the high performance industrial sector and application development capabilities that will help it respond quickly and effectively to customers' needs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition is expected to be immediately accretive to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's earnings per share and it will extend \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's portfolio of products, add new revenue streams, enhance production capacity and enable the combined company to leverage its strong customer relationships and partner network to expand distribution worldwide. Year one targeted synergies in raw materials, administrative areas and increasing aerospace revenue from added capacity are approximately US$15 million with additional synergies to be evaluated after closing. The estimated earnings per share accretion for the remainder of 2012 in respect of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's issued shares is approximately US$0.20 per share and full year 2013 is estimated at approximately US$0.65 per share including synergies.(*)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Upon completion of the Acquisition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  will organise the combined assets in two separate reporting segments. Umeco's advanced materials business will be integrated into a newly created High Performance Industrial Materials ("HPIM") segment that will focus on industrial and process materials growth segments. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Engineered Materials ("CEM") segment will continue to focus on aerospace growth opportunities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (*) These statements should not be interpreted to mean that earnings per share will necessarily be greater than in 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    4.         Background to, and reasons for, recommending the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following the disposal of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pattonair\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Supply Chain business, in July 2011, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been focused on its advanced composites business, which principally serves the aerospace and defence, wind energy, automotive, recreation and other industrial segments. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's focus within these end markets is those segments with underlying long term growth prospects, coupled with a propensity to switch to lighter weight high strength advanced composite materials driven by structural factors such as environmental regulation, rising fuel costs and safety considerations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following the good progress \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  has made with the execution of its growth strategy, the Board of Umeco received an initial approach from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  regarding a potential acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Following a number of subsequent discussions with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  , an enhanced proposal was received on 30 March 2012. During this time the Board of Umeco, in consultation with its advisors, has given careful consideration to the fundamental value of the business, taking into account \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's prospects in the growing global advanced composites market. The Board of Umeco believes that the offer from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is at a level which represents an attractive value for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  as well as providing an opportunity for Umeco Shareholders to realise the value of their entire investment in cash. Accordingly, the Board of Umeco intends to recommend that Umeco Shareholders vote in favour of the Scheme.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In arriving at their decision to recommend the Acquisition, the Board of Umeco has taken into account that the terms of the Acquisition represent a significant premium to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's share price immediately prior to this Announcement and to the average share price for the preceding three and six month periods, as detailed in paragraph 2 above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is focused on continuing to develop its product and applications technologies in the composites market. Accordingly, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  understands the strategic value in creating a larger advanced composites offering in the industrial applications segment, building on the success of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  business which has been developed to date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will therefore provide significant opportunities for the Umeco Group to expand its offering in the rapidly growing industrial markets for advanced composite materials through leveraging its customer service excellence, know-how and the combined entity's leading technologies within existing and new customer relationships.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    5.         Recommendation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Board of Umeco, which has been so advised by Rothschild and Investec, considers the terms of the Acquisition to be fair and reasonable. In providing financial advice to the Board of Umeco, Rothschild and Investec have taken into account the commercial assessments of the Board of Umeco. Rothschild and Investec are providing the independent financial advice for the purposes of Rule 3 of the Code and Investec is also acting as sole corporate broker to Umeco.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Accordingly, the Board of Umeco intends unanimously to recommend that Umeco Shareholders vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Special Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting to facilitate the implementation of the Scheme, as those members of the Board of Umeco who hold Umeco Shares have undertaken so to do in respect of their own beneficial holdings of 137,314 Umeco Shares (representing, in aggregate, approximately 0.3 per cent. of the Umeco Shares currently in issue).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    6.         Management, employees and locations of the Umeco Group \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  has assured the Board of Umeco that, upon the Scheme becoming effective, the existing employment rights, including pension rights, of the management and employees of the Umeco Group will be safeguarded.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that upon the Scheme becoming effective, the Chief Executive, Finance Director and each of the Non-executive Directors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will each resign from their office as a director of Umeco and, in respect of the Chief Executive and Finance Director, that they will resign as employees of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 . They will each receive compensation in line with their legal rights and the provisions of their respective service contracts or letters of appointment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Discussions between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's senior management in relation to any specific ongoing roles to be assigned to them in the enlarged group (following the Scheme becoming effective), and their ongoing terms of employment, may take place before the Acquisition has completed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  attaches great importance to the skills, experience and knowledge of the existing management and employees of the Umeco Group, who have contributed to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's success to date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whilst no detailed analysis has been undertaken, nor any firm opinions formed, the process of integration will likely include the closure of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's head office in the UK and may (subject to any applicable consultation process) result in a marginal reduction of headcount of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , when the business is combined with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  , and the possible redeployment of certain of the fixed assets of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and/or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends that the enlarged group will, nevertheless, seek to maintain an appropriately sized employee base in order to execute its growth plans whilst seeking to avoid unnecessary overlap with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's existing activities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    7.         Irrevocable undertakings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  has received irrevocable undertakings, inter alia, to vote in favour of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Special Resolution to be proposed at the General Meeting in respect of a total of 14,655,510 Umeco Shares (as at or around the date of this Announcement), representing, in aggregate, approximately 30.2 per cent. of the existing issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further details of these irrevocable undertakings (including further details of the circumstances in which they will lapse) are set out in Appendix III to this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    8.         Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  is an international provider of advanced composite materials primarily to the aerospace and defence, wind energy, automotive, recreation and other industrial segments. Following its incorporation in 1917, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  traded as a motor vehicle distributor in the south of England for many years before acquiring various businesses involved in the electrical and marine industries. In 1983, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  made its first entry into the aerospace sector when it acquired Fluid Transfer Limited, a manufacturer of aircraft refuelling equipment. This was followed in 1987 by the acquisition of Pattonair International Limited (subsequently renamed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pattonair Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  ), a specialist distributor of components to the aerospace sector. With a developing specialisation in the aerospace sector, the businesses involved in other industrial sectors were gradually divested. In 1994, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  was admitted to trading on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  . In 1997 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquired its first composite materials business and followed this with a series of acquisitions which formed the basis of the composites division. In 2011, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pattonair\f28 \uc2 \f2  business and therefore its business now comprises a focused composites business operating through two business streams: Structural Materials and Process Materials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Structural Materials\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Structural Materials business develops, manufactures and supplies high performance advanced composite materials. Structural Materials specialises in the manufacture of high performance composite materials for a diverse range of industries such as aerospace, marine, motor sport, automotive, construction, wind energy and leisure sports and has manufacturing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the UK, Germany and the US, and distributes its products worldwide. Customers include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus\f28 \uc2 \f2 , manufacturers of high performance supercars and Formula 1 teams.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Process Materials [ 12-04-12 0601GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Process Materials business develops, manufactures and supplies vacuum bagging materials to the composites industry and other markets, providing a wide range of materials and technical support to a growing number of international customers. Process Materials has manufacturing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Italy and France, a joint-venture manufacturing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in China, and has value-added distribution facilities in the UK and the US. It has a global distribution network. Customers include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing\f28 \uc2 \f2  and manufacturers of wind turbine blades.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Summarised financial information*\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In its financial year to 31 March 2011, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  generated revenue of GBP207.4m (2010: GBP174.8m), adjusted profit before tax of GBP16.4m (2010: GBP13.0m) and adjusted earnings per share of 24.6 pence (2010: 17.9 pence). Total dividends of 18.25 pence (2010: 17.50 pence) were paid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the six months to 30 September 2011, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  generated revenue of GBP105.7m (2010: GBP98.5m), adjusted profit before tax of GBP8.3m (2010: GBP7.7m) and adjusted earnings per share of 11.4 pence (2010: 11.4 pence). An interim dividend of 4.0 pence per share (2010: 6.75 pence) was declared and was paid to shareholders on 10 February 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  only (excluding \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pattonair\f28 \uc2 \f2  ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    9.         Information on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2   and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2   Bidco \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a global speciality chemicals and materials company focused on developing, manufacturing and selling value-added products. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's products serve a diverse range of end uses including aerospace composites, structural adhesives, automotive and industrial coatings, electronics, inks, mining and plastics. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  operates on a global basis with manufacturing and research facilities located in 14 countries. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  is listed on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  and has, as at the Business Day before the date of this Announcement, a market capitalisation of approximately US$2.6 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco is a private limited company incorporated in England and Wales which is an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco is itself a holding company that owns \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's UK operating company as well as interests in several other \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  European operating entities. Further details of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco will be contained in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10.        Offer-related arrangements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  entered into an agreement on 21 February 2012 (the "Confidentiality Agreement") pursuant to which, amongst other things, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  has undertaken to (i) keep confidential certain non-public information it receives relating to the Umeco Group, (ii) use such information solely for the purpose of evaluating a possible offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and (iii) not to disclose such information to third parties (other than certain permitted disclosees) unless required by law, regulation, a court of competent jurisdiction or any governmental or competent regulatory authority.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  has further undertaken that subject to certain limited exclusions, during the period of 12 months from the date of the Confidentiality Agreement, it will not directly or indirectly solicit, endeavour to entice away or offer to employ or to enter into any contract for services with any person who is (i) a director, company secretary, president, vice-president, general manager or a person with a similar level of responsibility, of any member of the Umeco Group or (ii) working for any member of the Umeco Group (whether as an employee or consultant or independent contractor) and who has been directly engaged in discussions regarding the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    11.        Financing arrangements for the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cash consideration payable under the terms of the Acquisition will be funded using \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco's existing cash resources. Further information on the financing of the Acquisition will be set out in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    12.        Cash confirmation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  , financial adviser to Cytec and Cytec Bidco, has confirmed that it is satisfied that sufficient financial resources are available to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco to enable it to satisfy, in full, the cash consideration payable to Umeco Shareholders under the terms of the Acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    13.        Umeco Share Schemes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Participants in the Umeco Share Schemes will be contacted separately regarding the effect of the Acquisition on their rights under the Umeco Share Schemes and appropriate proposals will be made to such persons in due course.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will extend to any Umeco Shares which are unconditionally allotted or issued before the Reduction Record Time as a result of the exercise of existing options or the vesting of awards under the Umeco Share Schemes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is proposed to amend the articles of association of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  at the General Meeting to provide that, if the Scheme becomes effective, any Umeco Shares issued (other than to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco or subsidiaries or nominees of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  ) between approval of the Scheme at the Court Meeting and the Reduction Record Time will be subject to the Scheme and that any Umeco Shares issued after the Reduction Record Time will automatically be acquired by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco in exchange for cash as described in paragraph 2 above on the same basis as under the Scheme. Consequently, participants in the Umeco Share Schemes whose rights to receive Umeco Shares under awards that vest after the Reduction Record Time will receive cash as described in paragraph 2 above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    14.        Disclosure of interests \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms that it is making on the date of this Announcement an Opening Position Disclosure, setting out the details required to be disclosed by it under Rule 8.1(a) of the Code.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As at the close of business on 11 April 2012, being the last practicable date prior to the publication of this Announcement, save as set out in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Opening Position Disclosure as referred to above and save for the irrevocable undertakings referred to in paragraph 7 above and set out in Appendix III to this Announcement, none of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco or any of their directors or any of their partners or, so far as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors are aware, any person acting, or deemed to be acting, in concert with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - had an interest in, or right to subscribe for, relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 ;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - had any short position in (whether conditional or absolute and whether in the money or otherwise), including any short position under a derivative, any agreement to sell or any delivery obligation or right to require another person to purchase or take delivery of, relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 ;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - had procured an irrevocable commitment or letter of intent to accept or vote in favour of the Acquisition in respect of relevant securities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; or\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - had borrowed or lent any Umeco Shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Furthermore, no arrangement exists with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco or any person acting in concert with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco in relation to Umeco Shares. For these purposes, an "arrangement" includes any indemnity or option arrangement, any agreement or any understanding, formal or informal, of whatever nature, relating to Umeco Shares which may be an inducement to deal or refrain from dealing in such securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    15.        Structure of the Acquisition \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is intended that the Acquisition will be effected by way of a Court-sanctioned scheme of arrangement under Part 26 of the Companies Act 2006. The Scheme is an arrangement between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Scheme Shareholders and is subject to the approval of the Court.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The purpose of the Scheme is to provide for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco to become the holder of the entire issued and to be issued ordinary share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This is to be achieved by the cancellation of the Scheme Shares and the application of the reserve arising from such cancellation in paying up in full a number of new shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  (which is equal, in nominal value, to the number of Scheme Shares cancelled) and issuing them to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco, in consideration of which the Scheme Shareholders will receive cash consideration on the basis set out in paragraph 2 of this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The implementation of the Scheme will be subject to the Conditions and certain further terms referred to in Appendix I to this Announcement and to be included in the Scheme Document. The Conditions in paragraph A of Appendix I to this Announcement provide that the Acquisition will lapse if:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - certain competition clearances are not obtained; or\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the Scheme does not become effective by 12 October 2012 (or such later date as may be agreed between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , with the consent of the Panel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In particular, to become effective, the Scheme requires the approval of Scheme Shareholders by the passing of a special resolution at the Court Meeting. The resolution must be approved by a majority in number present and voting at the Court Meeting, either in person or by proxy, representing not less than 75 per cent. in value of the Scheme Shares which are voted at the Court Meeting (or any adjournment thereof).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, to become effective, the Scheme also requires the passing at the General Meeting of a resolution to approve the Capital Reduction, certain amendments to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's articles of association and such other resolutions that may be necessary to implement the Scheme. This resolution requires the approval of Umeco Shareholders representing at least 75 per cent. of the votes cast at the General Meeting, which will be held immediately after the Court Meeting has been concluded or adjourned.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the necessary approvals of Umeco Shareholders have been obtained, and the other Conditions have been satisfied or (where applicable) waived, the Scheme must be sanctioned and the Capital Reduction confirmed by the Court. The Scheme will only become effective upon delivery to the Registrar of Companies of a copy of the order of the Court sanctioning the Scheme and the Statement of Capital attached to it. [ 12-04-12 0601GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Upon the Scheme becoming effective, it will be binding on all Scheme Shareholders, irrespective of whether or not they attended or voted at the Court Meeting or the General Meeting (and, if they attended and voted, whether or not they voted in favour). It is currently anticipated that the Scheme will become effective in the third quarter of 2012, subject to satisfaction or (where applicable) waiver of the Conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new ordinary shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be issued to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco pursuant to the Scheme will be issued fully paid and free from all liens, charges, equities, encumbrances, rights of pre-emption and any other interests of any nature whatsoever and together with all rights attaching thereto, including voting rights and the rights to receive and retain in full all dividends and other distributions declared, made or paid in or after the date of their issue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further details of the Scheme, including the expected timetable of the Scheme and how the Scheme Shareholders may participate in the Court Meeting and General Meeting, will be contained in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    16.        Overseas Shareholders \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The availability of the Acquisition or distribution of this Announcement to persons not resident in the United Kingdom may be prohibited or affected by the laws or regulations of their relevant jurisdiction. Such persons should inform themselves about, and observe, any applicable legal or regulatory requirements of their jurisdiction. Further details in relation to Overseas Shareholders will be contained in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    17.        De-listing \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An application will be made to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK Listing Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cancel the listing of the Umeco Shares on the Official List and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be requested to cancel trading of Umeco Shares on the Main Market of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  upon or shortly after the Effective Date. The last day of dealings in Umeco Shares on the Main Market of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to be the Business Day immediately prior to the Scheme Court Hearing and no transfers will be registered after 6:00 p.m. on that date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the Effective Date, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will become a wholly-owned subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco and share certificates in respect of Umeco Shares will cease to be valid and should be destroyed. In addition, entitlements to Umeco Shares held within the CREST system will be cancelled on the Effective Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is also proposed that, on or shortly after the Effective Date, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be re-registered as a private limited company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    18.        Anticipated timetable \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  currently anticipates that:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - it will publish and despatch the Scheme Document (including notices of the Shareholder Meetings) to Umeco Shareholders and, for information only, to participants in the Umeco Share Schemes as soon as is reasonably practicable and in any event within 28 days of the date of this Announcement (or such later date as may be agreed by the Panel);\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the Scheme will become effective in the third quarter of 2012, subject to the satisfaction (or, if applicable, waiver) of the Conditions set out in Appendix I to this Announcement; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the Long Stop Date for the Scheme to become effective and the Acquisition to be completed will be 12 October 2012, or such later date (if any) as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  may, with the consent of the Panel, agree and (if required) the Court may allow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The timing of events which relate to the implementation of the Acquisition is, however, subject to the approval of the Court and is therefore subject to change. Further details of the Scheme, including the expected timetable of the Scheme and how the Scheme Shareholders may participate in the Court Meeting and General Meeting, will be contained in the Scheme Document.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    19.        Documents on display \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Copies of the following documents will be made available on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  's websites at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.umeco.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.umeco.com}}}\uc2 \f2  and \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cytec.comrespectively"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cytec.comrespectively}}}\uc2 \f2  by no later than 12:00 p.m. (London time) on the Business Day following this Announcement until the end of the Offer Period:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - this Announcement;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the irrevocable undertakings referred to in paragraph 7 above and described in Appendix III to this Announcement; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the Confidentiality Agreement referred to in paragraph 10 above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    20.        \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  issued share capital \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In accordance with Rule 2.10 of the Code, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirms that as at the close of business on 11 April 2012, being the last Business Day prior to this Announcement, there were 48,489,133 Umeco Shares (ISIN GB0009116079) in issue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    21.        General \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will be made on the terms and subject to the conditions and further terms set out herein and in Appendix I to this Announcement and the further terms and conditions set out in the Scheme Document and Forms of Proxy when issued. The bases and sources of certain financial information contained in this Announcement are set out in Appendix II to this Announcement. A summary of the irrevocable undertakings given by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  Directors and the irrevocable undertakings given by certain other Umeco Shareholders is contained in Appendix III to this Announcement. Certain capitalised terms used in this Announcement are defined in Appendix IV to this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Acquisition will be subject to the applicable requirements of the Code, the Panel, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Financial Services Authority.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  reserves the right to elect, with the consent of the Panel, to implement the Acquisition by way of a Takeover Offer for the entire issued and to be issued share capital of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Umeco\f28 \uc2 \f2  not already held by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco as an alternative to the Scheme. In such an event a Takeover Offer will be implemented on the same terms (subject to appropriate amendments), so far as applicable, as those which would apply to the Scheme and subject to the amendment referred to in paragraph 6 of Part B of Appendix I to this Announcement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Acquisition is effected by way of a Takeover Offer and such offer becomes or is declared unconditional in all respects and sufficient acceptances are received in respect of such offer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cytec\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bidco intends to: (i) make an application to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK Listing Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cancel listing of the Umeco Shares on the Official List and request the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cancel trading of Umeco Shares on the Main Market; and (ii) exercise its rights (to the extent such rights are available) to apply the provisions of Chapter 3 of Part 28 of the Companies Act 2006 to acquire compulsorily the remaining Umeco Shares in respect of which such offer has not been accepted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  has given and has not withdrawn its written consent to the issue of this Announcement with the inclusion herein of the references to its name in the form and context in which it appears.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rothschild has given and has not withdrawn its written consent to the issue of this Announcement with the inclusion herein of the references to its name in the form and context in which it appears.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investec has given and has not withdrawn its written consent to the issue of this Announcement with the inclusion herein of the references to its name in the form and context in which it appears.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    22.        Investor and Analyst Presentation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There will be a \f28 \uc