\par\par \b \uc2 FXOUTLOOK-Yen falls after G7  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , traders eye 80 level\b0\par\par\uc2 876 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * G7 launches first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000\par \par \uc2 * Yen dives in Asia but decline eases in U.S., Europe\par \par \uc2 * Traders bracing for extended \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign\par \par \uc2 By Wanfeng Zhou\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 18 (Reuters) - Investors betting on a sustained decline in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be disappointed after the Group of Seven on Friday launched its first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000 and pledged to do more if needed to rein in a soaring yen.\par \par \uc2 Both the Federal Reserve and \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  said they had sold yen, bolstering European and Japanese efforts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and calm markets after Japan's devastating earthquake, tsunami and unfolding nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose nearly 4 percent to 82.00 yen on trading platform EBS <JPY=EBS> in European trade, but hedge funds and other speculative accounts tested official resolve by buying into the yen sell-off. The dollar last traded at 80.58 yen, though still up 2.4 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 "We still think that there will be appreciation pressure on the yen," said David Mann, head of research, Americas, at Standard Chartered in New York. "I would expect strong defense of 80. We can't rule out testing below that and then seeing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  push it back higher again."\par \par \uc2 C.J. Gavsie, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at BMO Capital Markets in Toronto, said since North American trading hours began, there had been "straightforward pressure to be buying yen and selling dollars, which is exactly the opposite" of what central banks were trying to achieve. As a result, the dollar quickly retreated below 81 yen.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo market estimates had the Bank of Japan selling some 2 trillion yen ($25 billion) over the course of the day. Nomura Securities estimated the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of about 5 billion euros ($7.1 billion).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  was estimated to have spent around C$100 million to C$150 million ($101.5 million to $152.3 million), according to BMO Capital.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that Japanese retail and corporate investors would start bringing money home for rebuilding after the disaster drove the yen up this week. So did heavy selling by margin traders who were forced to unwind positions funded with cheaply borrowed yen as risk aversion spiked.\par \par \uc2 While official yen-selling could continue for weeks, analysts emphasized that the main goal of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to reduce volatility but not necessarily to weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Central banks "want to make sure the speculative element is at a minimum," said David Watt, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto. "And they want to make sure that \b \highlight22\uc2 operationally\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market will always have another side."\par \par \uc2 YEN LONGS TO FALL\par \par \uc2 Net yen long positions rose to 30,230 contracts from last week's 16,656 contracts, data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission showed on Friday. Analysts expect yen longs to drop after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For more, see [ID:nN18138930]\par \par \uc2 Technical analysts noted upside targets around Monday's peak of 82.45, followed by the 100-day moving average of 82.61 and 83.30, the intraday high from last Friday. Nomura \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said the 82.70-83.00 range would be an "ideal level" for computer-driven model accounts to buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 Giuseppe Manieri, principal of Premium \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Advisors, said Friday's closing level is important. "If it is on the higher side of the weekly bar," it might mean a reversal.\par \par \uc2 "For now on the long-term side nothing has changed, the trend is still heavily downwards," he said. Zurich-based Premium \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Advisors has $875 million under management.\par \par \uc2 Paresh Upadhyaya, strategist at BofA \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 , said it may require a move toward higher interest rates in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sustain downward yen momentum.\par \par \uc2 "For \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be successful, it needs to be followed by policy action," he said. "If the Fed starts openly debating exiting quantitative easing, that would move interest rate differentials sharply in favor of the dollar against the yen."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 As the dollar rebounded, it became cheaper to hedge against further yen gains. Implied volatility on one-month dollar/yen options stood at 13.15 percent, down from 21 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ETF options, volume on the \b \highlight22\uc2 CurrencyShares\b0 \highlight\uc2  Japanese Yen Trust was four times the average daily turnover with about 15,000 puts and 5,811 calls traded, according to options analytics firm Trade Alert.\par \par \uc2 Options on the Proshares UltraShort Yen Fund turned busy for a second straight session. Overall volume of the fund was 6.6 times the average daily levels with about 13,000 calls and 430 puts traded on Friday, according to Trade Alert.\par \par \uc2 The euro hit a session high around 115.56 yen <EURJPY=R> before easing to 114.36, up about 3.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to a four-month high against the dollar of around $1.4185 <EUR=EBS> after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen. (Additional reporting by Steven C. Johnson and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss in New York, Doris Frankel in Chicago, Claire Sibonney and Ka Yan Ng in Toronto, and Martin de Sa'Pinto in Zurich; editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /OUTLOOK   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i001mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
