\par\par \b \uc2 ADR REPORT-Chilean ADRs fall after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chuck Mikolajczak   \par \uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 18:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Chilean shares traded in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  were sharply lower on Tuesday on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem strength in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank said on Monday it will buy $12 billion in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the peso, which has appreciated more than 17 percent against the U.S. dollar since the end of June, putting it near three-year highs. For details, see [ID:nN04206531] and [ID:nN03172599].\par \par \uc2 The move by the bank sent the Chilean peso <CLPUSD> down nearly 5 percent per dollar. The BNY Mellon index of leading Chilean ADRs <.BKCL> tumbled 3.5 percent. Receipts with the BNY Mellon index of leading Latin American ADRs <.BKLA> shed 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Shares traded in Chile were higher, but U.S. listed shares fell because the peso's decline has to be accounted for in the value of the ADRs.\par \par \uc2 U.S.-listed shares of Pension fund administrator \uc2 AFP Provida\uc2  slid 6.3 percent to $73.15 while financials Corpbanca dropped 6.4 percent to $87.79 and \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2  lost 3.2 percent to $90.77.\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon index of leading Asian ADRs <.BKAS> fell 0.9 percent on the first trading day of the year. In Asia, shares rose as investors bet on improving global economic data. [ID:nTOE703049] and [ID:nTOE70305W]\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon index of leading European ADRs <.BKEUR> edged up 0.2 percent, while Europe's FTSEurofirst 300 index of top shares <.FTEU3> gained almost 0.8 percent with miners and oil firms contributing to the bulk of gains as commodity prices were boosted by strong manufacturing data from around the world. [ID:nLDE7031G8]\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon index of leading American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) <.BKADR> dipped 0.3 percent while the U.S. benchmark S&P 500 index <.SPX> also shed 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-STOCKS-ADRS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|C|GRO|MTL|SOF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110104e714000yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
