\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan dlr surges after Fed stimulus; gains capped\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2010\par 03:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Monetary easing in United States boosts emerging mkt \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * T$ ends at highest price since July 31, 2008\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolls back most of the day's gains (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 TAIPEI, Nov 4 (Reuters) - Aggressive monetary easing by the United States lifted the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> to a new 28-month high on Thursday, but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the island's nervous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checked gains.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at T$30.59 per U.S. dollar, its strongest final price since July 31, 2008, and compared with Wednesday's close of T$30.65.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar's gains of more than 3 percent over the past six weeks and through Thursday stem from the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision to buy $600 billion in government bonds [ID:nN03163902].\par \par \uc2 Monetary easing is expected to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in fast-growing, emerging markets such as Taiwan, which offer higher returns than what their developed peers would offer.\par \par \uc2 "This is probably the path of least resistance in Asia right now and a confirmation of what's been building up over the past one to 1-\u189\'00\'BD months," said Emmanuel Ng, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with OCBC in Singapore. "It's going to serve as a backdrop."\par \par \uc2 Taiwan dollar prices on the main exchange had risen as high as T$30.24 in midday trade, while the smaller Cosmos <COSMOS1> exchange ended the session at T$30.245.\par \par \uc2 Differences between those prices and the day's close indicate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the main exchange to cap gains and limit volatility.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and consider capital controls if easing in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumps hot money into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, raising prices on exporters.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought about $6.1 billion in U.S. dollars since Sept. 27, according to an IFR Markets survey of traders.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0800 GMT         PREVIOUS SESSION CLOSE\par T$ (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 )      30.590                    30.650\par  T$ (Cosmos1)           30.245                    30.405\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  is Taiwan's main \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange; Cosmos is a\par small exchange.\par NDFs (vs U.S. dollar)\par                0800 GMT          PREVIOUS SESSION, 0828 GMT\par  6-month       T$29.883                       T$29.975\par  2-year        T$29.033                       T$29.270\par Net foreign trading in Taiwan stocks (T$ bln)\par    Thursday              Month to date               October\par       8.608                  50.483                   40.372\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (See [EMRG/FRX] for a table of year-to-date Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance.) (Reporting by Ralph Jennings; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -TAIWAN/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Do